; Lowering — real instruction emission for the tagged-`Int` ABI (spec
; §2.2/§3.4), replacing slice 2B/2G's constant-folding evaluator entirely.
;
; ## What changed, and why
;
; The previous version of this module (`FoldVal`, `fold-expr`, …) never
; wrote a single LLVM instruction: it *evaluated* `main`'s body down to
; one compile-time `Int` and handed that number to `bc-writer.mnd`'s
; `write-int-main-bc`, which always produced `define i32 @main() { ret
; i32 N }` — a correct exit code, but a `.bc` whose instructions do not
; compute anything. That was a deliberate, documented shortcut for
; slices 2B/2G (see the plan for exactly what it bought); this slice
; replaces it with a real (if still narrow) instruction selector: `Int`
; literals, `+ - * / %`, comparisons, `if`, `let` (both shapes), `do`, and
; calls to other top-level `Int`-returning `defn`s all become real
; `alloca`/`store`/`load`/`binop`/`icmp`/`br`/`call`/`ret` instructions
; (`src/emit/llvm-ir.mnd`'s `Item`s), assembled into an `LlvmModule` and
; handed to `src/emit/bc-writer.mnd`'s `write-module-bc`. `FoldVal` and
; every `fold-*` function are gone; there is no more "evaluate the
; program inside the compiler" path at all.
;
; What is *not* lowered here — `match`, `fn` (a closure
; `close/close.mnd` failed to lambda-lift), and any value that isn't
; `Int` (`Bool` as a first-class value, `Str`, lists, records, other
; `variant`s) — is a clean `Err`, not a crash and not a silent
; miscompile; see "Scope" below for exactly what that means for each.
; `loop`/`recur` over Int bindings *are* lowered (slice 3A).
;
; ## The tagged-`Int` ABI, literally
;
; Every `Int` this module ever produces a value for is the *tagged*
; representation, `t(v) = (v << 1) | 1` (`runtime/include/menard.h`),
; held in an `i64`. Two operations are free (spec §2.2): `+`/`-` on the
; tagged words directly, fixed up by one extra `add`/`sub` of the
; constant `1` (`t(a) + t(b) - 1 == t(a + b)`; `t(a) - t(b) + 1 == t(a -
; b)`) — the fixup is *not* optional, and skipping it is exactly the
; "naive tagged multiply" mistake spec §2.2 calls out (for `+`/`-` the
; fixup is required for correctness, not an optimisation). `*`/`/`/`%`
; untag both operands (`ashr 1`, sign-extending), perform the native
; 64-bit op, then retag (`shl 1`, `or 1`). `/` and `%` check the
; divisor first and call `mn_panic` when it is zero (spec §3.4).
; Comparisons (`< > <= >= =`) run directly on the tagged words
; (tagging is order- and equality-preserving, an injective affine map, so
; no untagging is needed) and produce `i1`, consumed only by `if`'s own
; conditional branch — this module has no other way to produce or
; consume a `Bool` value (see "Scope").
;
; ## `Builder`: the one piece of mutable state per function
;
; Exactly one `Builder` is threaded through lowering one function's body
; (never shared across functions). It owns three `Ref`s:
;
; - `items`: every `Item` appended so far, **in reverse** (`Cons`ed onto
;   the front — O(1) — then reversed once, at the end, into the order
;   `LFunc`/`write-module-bc` need).
; - `next-val`: the running absolute SSA value-id counter. A function's
;   own params occupy the first `nparams` ids right after every
;   module-scope global value (`num-globals` — the total count of
;   `Int`-returning top-level `defn`s, fixed once for the whole module
;   before any function body is lowered); `builder-new` is handed
;   `num-globals + nparams` as this counter's starting point, i.e. *after*
;   the params, since params never themselves appear as an `Item` (they
;   are simply referenced by their fixed ids). Each value-producing `Item`
;   consumes exactly one id, at the moment it is appended (`bump-val!`).
; - `next-bb`: the next not-yet-used basic-block index (`fresh-bb!`);
;   block 0 (the entry block) is implicitly already "current" the moment
;   a `Builder` is created, so this starts at `1`. See `llvm-ir.mnd`'s
;   "Basic blocks are implicit" note: nothing here tracks "which block is
;   currently open" beyond this counter — a new block simply begins right
;   after whatever `Item` most recently terminated one (`IBr`/`ICondBr`/
;   `IRet`), which holds automatically as long as every `if`'s `then`
;   block's `Item`s are fully appended before its `else` block's, which
;   are fully appended before `join`'s — exactly the order `lower-if`
;   below produces by simple recursive-descent structure, with no explicit
;   block bookkeeping needed beyond the three fresh indices it allocates.
;
; Every relative-value-reference computation (`rel-ref`) reads `next-val`
; *at the moment an instruction is appended*, before that instruction's
; own result (if it has one) is counted — exactly the semantics module
; format version 1 needs (`nextValueNo - targetAbsoluteId`; see
; `bc-writer.mnd`'s and `tools/bc-writer/write-ssa.ts`'s header comments
; for how this was confirmed against a real bitcode reader).
;
; ## Constants are never cached across a function — a real bug, fixed once
;
; An earlier draft of this module (and of `tools/bc-writer/write-ssa.ts`,
; where the mistake was actually caught) tried to dedupe small constants
; per function — "the tagged `1` is always the same value, so intern it
; once and reuse its id everywhere". That is wrong the moment the first
; use is inside an `if`'s `then` branch and a later use is inside its
; `else` sibling: `then` does not dominate `else`, so a value defined
; there is not valid there, and the module fails to verify (or worse,
; behaves unpredictably in a toolchain that skips verification). The fix
; kept here is the simple, always-correct one: `const-i64!`/`const-i32!`
; below never cache anything — every call materializes a brand-new
; `IConstI64`/`IConstI32` `Item`, right at the point of use, in whichever
; block is currently being appended to. This costs a little bitcode size
; (the same small integer may appear several times) and costs nothing in
; correctness: a freshly created value trivially dominates its own,
; immediately-following use, unconditionally, regardless of what control
; flow is or isn't open around it.
;
; ## Locals: `alloca` + `store`/`load`, uniformly, for params too
;
; Spec §3.4 "emit naive IR; let LLVM optimise" — this module allocates one
; `i64` slot per bound name (a `defn`'s own parameters *and* every `let`),
; stores into it once, and reads it back with a fresh `load` at every
; reference, never reusing a cached SSA value across uses the way a
; smarter frontend would. `mem2reg` (run by `clang`/`opt`, never by this
; compiler) turns every one of these into real SSA once the module is
; loaded; this module's own job is only to be *obviously correct*, not
; small. `env`, threaded through every lowering function below, maps a
; bound name to its alloca's absolute value id (never to a raw value) —
; `lower-sym` is the one place that turns a name into a value, via `load`.
;
; ## `if`, without hand-built `phi`s
;
; `lower-if` allocates a temporary result slot (another `alloca`, in the
; block open when the `if` is encountered — which dominates `then`,
; `else` and `join` alike), lowers `then` into a fresh `then` block ending
; in a `store` to that slot and a `br` to `join`, lowers `else` into a
; fresh `else` block the same way, then `load`s the slot back in `join` —
; exactly spec §3.4's "no hand-built phi nodes, no dominance-frontier
; reasoning" instruction, at the cost of one extra `alloca`/`store`/`load`
; per `if` that `mem2reg` is expected to clean up later, not by this
; compiler.
;
; ## Calls, and the two kinds of top-level `defn` this module sees
;
; After `close/close.mnd` (lambda lifting) and `root/root.mnd` (shadow-
; stack wrapping) have run, every top-level `defn` a real program's forms
; contain is one of exactly two shapes:
;
; - An **`Int`-only `defn`** (every param and the return both a bare
;   `Int`): `main`, any user-written helper, and every lambda-lifted
;   `__lamN`. Every one of these becomes a real `i64`-params-and-return
;   `LFunc` (`main` alone gets `() -> i32`, spec's C entry point — see
;   `finish-main-return!` below) — `collect-int-defns`/`build-func-refs`
;   assign each one a module-scope global value id, `0..N-1`, in the
;   order they appear in the program's top-level forms (this fixes the
;   global numbering `ICall`'s callee-rel operands are computed against —
;   see `llvm-ir.mnd`'s "order fixes each function's... id" note; it must
;   match `write-module-bc`'s own traversal of the same list exactly, and
;   does, since both walk the one `LFunc` list this module builds).
; - A **`Unit`, zero-parameter, empty-body no-op `defn`** — precisely
;   `root/root.mnd`'s own `shadow-push`/`shadow-pop` stand-ins (spec §4.4's
;   shadow-stack rooting ABI, still a no-op in phase 2 — see that module's
;   header comment and `runtime/src/shadow.c`'s). This module never lowers
;   these to a real function at all: `collect-noop-names` recognises the
;   shape structurally (not by hardcoding the two names), and
;   `lower-sequence` simply *skips* a call to one wherever it appears in a
;   body sequence (always mid-sequence, never a body's last form, by
;   `root/root.mnd`'s own construction) — no `LFunc`, no `ICall`, nothing
;   in the emitted module at all for either helper.
;
; Any *other* call — to a name that is neither of the above (a `Bool`-
; returning helper, a constructor, an unresolved free variable, …) — is a
; clean `Err`.
;
; ## Scope: what is not lowered, and why that is an `Err`, not a fallback
;
; - **`match`, `fn`.** `match` needs a real heap-object/shape-descriptor
;   model (spec §2.2's tagged-pointer objects) this backend has no
;   allocator story for at all; a leftover `fn` means `close-convert`
;   failed to lambda-lift it (its own documented limitation). Rather than
;   half-implement any of these, every one is a named, explicit `Err`.
;   `loop`/`recur` *are* lowered (slice 3A: alloca bindings, header/exit
;   blocks, parallel `recur` assignment).
; - **`Bool`/`Unit` as first-class values (slice 3B).** Spec §2.2 leaves
;   the bit patterns unspecified; Int already occupies every odd residue
;   via `t(v)=(v<<1)|1`, so this module uses the type-erased immediates
;   `false`/`Unit` = 1 and `true` = 3 (same bits as `t(0)`/`t(1)`).
;   Comparisons as values zext the `i1` and retag; `if`'s test accepts
;   either a direct comparison or any Bool-valued expression (`icmp ne`
;   against `false`). `Int`/`Bool`/`Unit` params and returns share the
;   same `i64` word ABI (alloca/store/load).
; - **`sdiv`/`srem`-by-zero guard (spec §3.4).** `/` and `%` untag, then
;   branch on a zero divisor to a block that calls `mn_panic` with
;   `"division by zero"` and ends in `unreachable`. The success block
;   does the native op and retags. LLVM's `sdiv`/`srem` by zero is
;   undefined, so the check has to be explicit.

(import "../reader/ast.mnd")
(import "../pool/pool.mnd")
(import "../util/result.mnd")
(import "./llvm-ir.mnd")
(import "./bc-writer.mnd")
(import std/list)

(pub alias Ast Ast)
(pub alias Span Span)
(pub alias Imp Imp)

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Small Ast helpers, restated locally per `src/`'s "no prelude import"
; rule (see `type/check.mnd`'s equivalent header note).

(defn sym-str (ast: Ast) -> (Maybe Str)
  (match ast (SymNode n _) (Some n) _ (None)))

(defn is-sym (ast: Ast) (name: Str) -> Bool
  (match (sym-str ast) (Some n) (= n name) (None) false))

(defn strip-trailing-colon (raw: Str) -> Str
  (let n (str-byte-length raw))
  (if (and (> n 0) (= (str-byte raw (- n 1)) 58)) (str-slice raw 0 (- n 1)) raw))

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; `defn` header parsing: name, `(name: Type)` params (both parts kept —
; unlike the old fold-based lowerer, this module needs a param's declared
; type to decide whether the whole `defn` is lowerable at all), the
; return type, and the body.

(defrec LParam (name: Str) (ty: Ast))
(defn lparam-name (p: LParam) -> Str (match p (LParam n _) n))
(defn lparam-ty (p: LParam) -> Ast (match p (LParam _ t) t))

(defrec LDefn (name: Str) (params: (List LParam)) (ret: Ast) (body: (List Ast)))
(defn ldefn-name (ld: LDefn) -> Str (match ld (LDefn n _ _ _) n))
(defn ldefn-params (ld: LDefn) -> (List LParam) (match ld (LDefn _ p _ _) p))
(defn ldefn-ret (ld: LDefn) -> Ast (match ld (LDefn _ _ r _) r))
(defn ldefn-body (ld: LDefn) -> (List Ast) (match ld (LDefn _ _ _ b) b))

(defn param-arity-of (ps: (List LParam)) -> Int
  (match ps [] 0 (Cons _ rest) (+ 1 (param-arity-of rest))))

(defn lparam-names (ps: (List LParam)) -> (List Str)
  (match ps [] [] (Cons p rest) (Cons (lparam-name p) (lparam-names rest))))

(defrec ArrowSplit (before: (List Ast)) (after: (List Ast)))

(defn find-arrow (elems: (List Ast)) -> (Maybe ArrowSplit)
  (match elems
    [] (None)
    (Cons e rest) (find-arrow-cons e rest)))

(defn find-arrow-cons (e: Ast) (rest: (List Ast)) -> (Maybe ArrowSplit)
  (if (is-sym e "->") (Some (ArrowSplit [] rest))
    (find-arrow-cons-recurse e rest)))

(defn find-arrow-cons-recurse (e: Ast) (rest: (List Ast)) -> (Maybe ArrowSplit)
  (match (find-arrow rest)
    (None) (None)
    (Some split) (Some (ArrowSplit (Cons e (arrow-split-before split)) (arrow-split-after split)))))

(defn arrow-split-before (s: ArrowSplit) -> (List Ast) (match s (ArrowSplit b _) b))
(defn arrow-split-after (s: ArrowSplit) -> (List Ast) (match s (ArrowSplit _ a) a))

(defn param-of (ast: Ast) -> (Maybe LParam)
  (match ast
    (ParenNode (Cons name-ast (Cons ty-ast _)) _) (param-of-named name-ast ty-ast)
    _ (None)))

(defn param-of-named (name-ast: Ast) (ty-ast: Ast) -> (Maybe LParam)
  (match (sym-str name-ast)
    (Some n) (Some (LParam (strip-trailing-colon n) ty-ast))
    (None) (None)))

(defn params-of (elems: (List Ast)) -> (List LParam)
  (match elems
    [] []
    (Cons e rest) (params-of-cons e rest)))

(defn params-of-cons (e: Ast) (rest: (List Ast)) -> (List LParam)
  (match (param-of e)
    (Some p) (Cons p (params-of rest))
    (None) (params-of rest)))

; `main` or `(f [a])` — the type-parameter list (if any) is irrelevant
; here (this lowerer never instantiates one), only the bare name is.
(defn defn-name-of (name-part: Ast) -> (Maybe Str)
  (match name-part
    (SymNode n _) (Some n)
    (ParenNode (Cons n-ast _) _) (sym-str n-ast)
    _ (None)))

(defn parse-ldefn (elems: (List Ast)) -> (Maybe LDefn)
  (match elems
    (Cons _ (Cons name-part rest)) (parse-ldefn-named name-part rest)
    _ (None)))

(defn parse-ldefn-named (name-part: Ast) (rest: (List Ast)) -> (Maybe LDefn)
  (match (defn-name-of name-part)
    (None) (None)
    (Some name) (parse-ldefn-header name rest)))

(defn parse-ldefn-header (name: Str) (rest: (List Ast)) -> (Maybe LDefn)
  (match (find-arrow rest)
    (None) (None)
    (Some split) (parse-ldefn-ret name (params-of (arrow-split-before split)) (arrow-split-after split))))

(defn parse-ldefn-ret (name: Str) (params: (List LParam)) (after: (List Ast)) -> (Maybe LDefn)
  (match after
    (Cons ret-ast body) (Some (LDefn name params ret-ast body))
    [] (None)))

; `(pub defn …)` — strip the `pub` wrapper; every other top-level shape
; (`defrec`, `variant`, `alias`, a bare expression, …) is not a `defn` and
; is simply not a lowering-relevant form.
(defn unwrap-pub (ast: Ast) -> Ast
  (match ast
    (ParenNode (Cons head rest) sp) (unwrap-pub-head head rest sp ast)
    _ ast))

(defn unwrap-pub-head (head: Ast) (rest: (List Ast)) (sp: Span) (ast: Ast) -> Ast
  (if (is-sym head "pub") (unwrap-pub (ParenNode rest sp)) ast))

(defn top-form-ldefn (ast: Ast) -> (Maybe LDefn)
  (match (unwrap-pub ast)
    (ParenNode (Cons head rest) _) (top-form-ldefn-named head rest)
    _ (None)))

(defn top-form-ldefn-named (head: Ast) (rest: (List Ast)) -> (Maybe LDefn)
  (if (is-sym head "defn") (parse-ldefn (Cons head rest)) (None)))

(defn collect-ldefns-all (forms: (List Ast)) -> (List LDefn)
  (match forms
    [] []
    (Cons f rest) (collect-ldefns-all-cons f rest)))

(defn collect-ldefns-all-cons (f: Ast) (rest: (List Ast)) -> (List LDefn)
  (match (top-form-ldefn f)
    (None) (collect-ldefns-all rest)
    (Some ld) (Cons ld (collect-ldefns-all rest))))

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Which top-level `defn`s this module actually lowers — see header
; comment's "Calls, and the two kinds of top-level `defn`".

(defn is-type-named (ast: Ast) (name: Str) -> Bool
  (match ast (SymNode n _) (= n name) _ false))

(defn is-int-type (ast: Ast) -> Bool (is-type-named ast "Int"))
(defn is-bool-type (ast: Ast) -> Bool (is-type-named ast "Bool"))
(defn is-unit-type (ast: Ast) -> Bool (is-type-named ast "Unit"))

; One-word immediates share the `i64` ABI (slice 3B).
(defn is-word-type (ast: Ast) -> Bool
  (or (is-int-type ast) (is-bool-type ast) (is-unit-type ast)))

; Heap object types are still one `i64` word (a pointer) — List/Maybe/Result
; for slice 3C; more shapes land in later slices. User nominals (`Ast`,
; `Span`, `Type`, …) are the same ABI: a tagged heap pointer in an `i64`.
; After private-symbol uniquify, names look like `__m3_Span` — strip the
; `__mN_` prefix before the Upper-initial check.
(defn is-raw-upper-name (n: Str) -> Bool
  (and (> (str-byte-length n) 0)
    (do
      (let b (str-byte n 0))
      (and (>= b 65) (<= b 90)))))

; `__m12_Foo` → `Foo`; otherwise identity.
(defn strip-uniq-prefix (n: Str) -> Str
  (do
    (let len (str-byte-length n))
    (if (and (>= len 4) (= (str-byte n 0) 95) (= (str-byte n 1) 95) (= (str-byte n 2) 109))
      (strip-uniq-prefix-digits n 3 len)
      n)))

(defn strip-uniq-prefix-digits (n: Str) (i: Int) (len: Int) -> Str
  (if (>= i len) n
    (do
      (let b (str-byte n i))
      (if (and (>= b 48) (<= b 57))
        (strip-uniq-prefix-digits n (+ i 1) len)
        (if (= b 95) (str-slice n (+ i 1) (- len (+ i 1))) n)))))

(defn is-upper-type-name (n: Str) -> Bool
  (is-raw-upper-name (strip-uniq-prefix n)))

(defn is-heap-type (ast: Ast) -> Bool
  (match ast
    (SymNode n _) (is-upper-type-name n)
    (ParenNode (Cons head _) _) (is-heap-type-head head)
    _ false))

(defn is-heap-type-head (head: Ast) -> Bool
  (match (sym-str head)
    (Some n)
      (or (= n "List")
          (= n "Maybe")
          (= n "Result")
          (= n "Ref")
          (= n "Map")
          (= n "Fn")
          (is-upper-type-name n))
    (None) false))

(defn is-str-type (ast: Ast) -> Bool (is-type-named ast "Str"))
(defn is-sb-type (ast: Ast) -> Bool (is-type-named ast "StringBuffer"))

; A declared type parameter (`a` in `(defn (f [a]) …)`) is one word too.
; The lowerer emits one body and never instantiates, so `a` has the same
; ABI as `Int` or `(List a)`.
(defn is-type-var (ast: Ast) -> Bool
  (match ast
    (SymNode n _)
      (and (> (str-byte-length n) 0)
        (do
          (let b (str-byte n 0))
          (and (>= b 97) (<= b 122)
            (not (or (= n "Int") (= n "Bool") (= n "Unit") (= n "Str"))))))
    _ false))

(defn is-value-type (ast: Ast) -> Bool
  (or (is-word-type ast) (is-heap-type ast) (is-str-type ast) (is-sb-type ast) (is-type-var ast)))

(defn all-params-value (ps: (List LParam)) -> Bool
  (match ps [] true (Cons p rest) (and (is-value-type (lparam-ty p)) (all-params-value rest))))

; Empty Unit no-ops (`shadow-push`/`shadow-pop`) stay out of the emitted
; function list — see `is-unit-noop-ldefn` below.
(defn is-word-ldefn (ld: LDefn) -> Bool
  (if (is-unit-noop-ldefn ld) false
    (and (is-value-type (ldefn-ret ld)) (all-params-value (ldefn-params ld)))))

(defn filter-word-ldefns (lds: (List LDefn)) -> (List LDefn)
  (match lds
    [] []
    (Cons ld rest) (filter-word-ldefns-cons ld rest)))

(defn filter-word-ldefns-cons (ld: LDefn) (rest: (List LDefn)) -> (List LDefn)
  (if (is-word-ldefn ld) (Cons ld (filter-word-ldefns rest)) (filter-word-ldefns rest)))

; `root/root.mnd`'s `shadow-helper-defn` builds exactly `(defn NAME ->
; Unit ())` — a single-form body that is itself the empty-parens `Unit`
; literal `()` (an empty `ParenNode`), not an empty body list.
(defn is-unit-literal (ast: Ast) -> Bool
  (match ast (ParenNode [] _) true _ false))

(defn is-unit-literal-body (body: (List Ast)) -> Bool
  (match body [f] (is-unit-literal f) _ false))

(defn is-unit-noop-ldefn (ld: LDefn) -> Bool
  (and (is-unit-type (ldefn-ret ld))
       (match (ldefn-params ld) [] true _ false)
       (is-unit-literal-body (ldefn-body ld))))

(defn collect-noop-names (lds: (List LDefn)) -> (Map Str Bool)
  (match lds
    [] (map-new)
    (Cons ld rest) (collect-noop-names-cons ld rest)))

(defn collect-noop-names-cons (ld: LDefn) (rest: (List LDefn)) -> (Map Str Bool)
  (if (is-unit-noop-ldefn ld)
    (map-set (collect-noop-names rest) (ldefn-name ld) true)
    (collect-noop-names rest)))

(defn find-ldefn-named (lds: (List LDefn)) (name: Str) -> (Maybe LDefn)
  (match lds
    [] (None)
    (Cons ld rest) (if (= (ldefn-name ld) name) (Some ld) (find-ldefn-named rest name))))

; A resolved call target: its module-scope global value id and its
; declared arity (for the arity check `lower-call-with-ref` below does).
(defrec FuncRef (abs: Int) (arity: Int))
(defn func-ref-abs (fr: FuncRef) -> Int (match fr (FuncRef a _) a))
(defn func-ref-arity (fr: FuncRef) -> Int (match fr (FuncRef _ a) a))

(defn build-func-refs (lds: (List LDefn)) (idx: Int) -> (Map Str FuncRef)
  (match lds
    [] (map-new)
    (Cons ld rest) (map-set (build-func-refs rest (+ idx 1)) (ldefn-name ld) (FuncRef idx (param-arity-of (ldefn-params ld))))))

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; `Builder` — see header comment's "The one piece of mutable state per
; function".

; A basic block is its own independent, mutable slot; a value like
; `IBr`'s target is only known once that block is **closed** (see below)
; — not the instant it is allocated. Two attempts at a simpler design
; were tried and both broke the moment a branch's own content was
; itself another `if` (both are recorded here since either mistake is
; easy to make again):
;
; 1. One shared flat `items` list, with `IBr`/`ICondBr` targets computed
;    as plain absolute block numbers *the moment `fresh-bb!` hands them
;    out* — before `then`/`else` are lowered at all. Nested control flow
;    allocates *more* blocks while `then` is still being lowered, and
;    those ids land, in the actual output stream, in between `then`'s
;    own content and `else`'s — but `else`'s target id was already
;    fixed to a number that assumed no such thing would happen. Caught
;    by `llvm-as`'s "does not dominate all uses", one step removed from
;    the real mistake.
; 2. Giving every block its *own* separate item-slot (fixing #1's
;    branch-target mismatch) but still assigning each slot's final
;    stream position at *allocation* time. This looked right — every
;    branch target now really does point at the block it means — but
;    broke *value* numbering instead: `next-val` counts up in the literal
;    call order lowering happens to run in (`then`'s whole nested subtree
;    finishes — including blocks allocated *after* `else`/`join` were —
;    before `else` is even started), while `write-module-bc` reads the
;    flattened stream in allocation-position order. The two orders only
;    coincide when there is no nesting at all; a nested `if` proved it
;    silently miscounts value ids (`llvm-dis`'s "Invalid store record").
;
; The fix actually kept here: a block's final stream position is decided
; not at allocation, and not by a separately-chosen layout, but at
; **closure** — the moment lowering is done with it and moves on
; (`switch-to!`, or the one implicit close of whatever block is still
; open when the function itself is finished, `finish-builder!`). Closure
; order, it turns out, is *exactly* call order: a block's own content is
; always one contiguous burst of `emit!`/`bump-val!` calls between the
; moment it becomes current and the moment something switches away from
; it, so numbering blocks in the order they close reproduces the same
; order `next-val` already counts up in — value numbering and block
; numbering agree again, at any nesting depth, with no separate
; "layout" decision to get right or wrong.
;
; That leaves branch targets referencing a block that has not closed
; yet (every branch here is a forward reference — `if`'s `condbr` always
; targets `then`/`else`, neither closed; `then`'s and `else`'s own `br`s
; always target `join`, closed last of the three). A block's `BB` handle
; therefore carries its index as a `Ref Int`, unresolved (`-1`) until
; `close-current!` fills it in; `IBr`/`ICondBr` cannot be finished at the
; moment they are appended (their target's `Ref Int` has no real value
; yet), so this module keeps its own `PendingItem` — everything else is
; already a finished `Item`, but a branch instead carries the *handle*
; it will resolve against once every block has finally closed, at
; `builder-items-ordered`'s call to `resolve-pending-list`.
(variant PendingItem
  (PDone Item)
  (PBr (Ref Int))
  (PCondBr (Ref Int) (Ref Int) Int))

(defrec BB (idx-ref: (Ref Int)) (slot: (Ref (List PendingItem))))
(defn bb-idx-ref (bb: BB) -> (Ref Int) (match bb (BB r _) r))
(defn bb-slot (bb: BB) -> (Ref (List PendingItem)) (match bb (BB _ s) s))

; `loop`/`recur` (slice 3A) need two more pieces of per-function mutable
; state, threaded alongside everything above:
;
; - `terminated`: true exactly when the block currently open already
;   ends in a terminator (`IBr`/`ICondBr`/`IRet`) — `emit-br!`/
;   `emit-condbr!`/`emit-ret!` set it, `switch-to!` clears it the moment
;   a *different*, freshly-open block becomes current. Two LLVM
;   instructions can never share a block if the first is already a
;   terminator; `recur` (which br's straight back to its loop's header)
;   and `if` (whose `then`/`else` arm might itself be a `recur`, or end
;   in one several levels of nested `if`/`loop` down) both need to know,
;   right where they finish lowering a branch's value, whether the
;   block they are about to append a `store`+`br` to is still open at
;   all — see `maybe-store-and-br!` below.
; - `loops`: the stack of enclosing `LoopFrame`s (innermost first), so
;   `recur` can find which loop it targets (`current-loop-frame`) and
;   `lower-loop`/`lower-recur` can push/pop as loops nest.
(defrec LoopFrame (header: BB) (exit-bb: BB) (result-slot: Int) (slots: (List Int)) (names: (List Str)) (root-mark: Int))
(defn loop-frame-header (lf: LoopFrame) -> BB (match lf (LoopFrame h _ _ _ _ _) h))
(defn loop-frame-exit-bb (lf: LoopFrame) -> BB (match lf (LoopFrame _ e _ _ _ _) e))
(defn loop-frame-result-slot (lf: LoopFrame) -> Int (match lf (LoopFrame _ _ r _ _ _) r))
(defn loop-frame-slots (lf: LoopFrame) -> (List Int) (match lf (LoopFrame _ _ _ s _ _) s))
(defn loop-frame-names (lf: LoopFrame) -> (List Str) (match lf (LoopFrame _ _ _ _ n _) n))
(defn loop-frame-root-mark (lf: LoopFrame) -> Int (match lf (LoopFrame _ _ _ _ _ m) m))

(defrec Builder (closed: (Ref (List (Ref (List PendingItem))))) (cur: (Ref BB)) (next-val: (Ref Int)) (closed-count: (Ref Int)) (terminated: (Ref Bool)) (loops: (Ref (List LoopFrame))) (rooting: (Ref Bool)) (root-base: (Ref Int)) (root-ns: (Ref Int)))

(defn b-closed (b: Builder) -> (Ref (List (Ref (List PendingItem)))) (match b (Builder c _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _) c))
(defn b-cur (b: Builder) -> (Ref BB) (match b (Builder _ c _ _ _ _ _ _ _) c))
(defn b-next-val (b: Builder) -> (Ref Int) (match b (Builder _ _ n _ _ _ _ _ _) n))
(defn b-closed-count (b: Builder) -> (Ref Int) (match b (Builder _ _ _ n _ _ _ _ _) n))
(defn b-terminated (b: Builder) -> (Ref Bool) (match b (Builder _ _ _ _ t _ _ _ _) t))
(defn b-loops (b: Builder) -> (Ref (List LoopFrame)) (match b (Builder _ _ _ _ _ l _ _ _) l))
(defn b-rooting (b: Builder) -> (Ref Bool) (match b (Builder _ _ _ _ _ _ r _ _) r))
(defn b-root-base (b: Builder) -> (Ref Int) (match b (Builder _ _ _ _ _ _ _ r _) r))
(defn b-root-ns (b: Builder) -> (Ref Int) (match b (Builder _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ n) n))

(defn new-bb -> BB (BB (ref (- 1)) (ref [])))

(defn builder-new (start-val: Int) -> Builder
  (Builder (ref []) (ref (new-bb)) (ref start-val) (ref 0) (ref false) (ref []) (ref false) (ref 0) (ref 0)))

(defn block-terminated? (b: Builder) -> Bool (deref (b-terminated b)))
(defn mark-terminated! (b: Builder) -> Unit (set! (b-terminated b) true))

(defn push-loop-frame! (b: Builder) (lf: LoopFrame) -> Unit
  (set! (b-loops b) (Cons lf (deref (b-loops b)))))

(defn pop-loop-frame! (b: Builder) -> Unit
  (set! (b-loops b) (match (deref (b-loops b)) [] [] (Cons _ rest) rest)))

(defn current-loop-frame (b: Builder) -> (Maybe LoopFrame)
  (match (deref (b-loops b)) [] (None) (Cons lf _) (Some lf)))

(defn emit-pending! (b: Builder) (p: PendingItem) -> Unit
  (do
    (let cur (deref (b-cur b)))
    (let slot (bb-slot cur))
    (set! slot (Cons p (deref slot)))))

(defn emit! (b: Builder) (it: Item) -> Unit (emit-pending! b (PDone it)))

(defn rel-ref (b: Builder) (abs-id: Int) -> Int
  (- (deref (b-next-val b)) abs-id))

(defn bump-val! (b: Builder) -> Int
  (do
    (let v (deref (b-next-val b)))
    (set! (b-next-val b) (+ v 1))
    v))

; Allocates a fresh, still-open block; call `switch-to!` once lowering
; actually reaches it (its final index stays unresolved until then).
(defn fresh-bb! (b: Builder) -> BB (new-bb))

; Closes whichever block is currently open: resolves *its* index to the
; running closure-order counter, files its slot away in closure order,
; then bumps the counter — see header comment's "closure order ... is
; exactly call order".
(defn close-current! (b: Builder) -> Unit
  (do
    (let cur (deref (b-cur b)))
    (let n (deref (b-closed-count b)))
    (set! (bb-idx-ref cur) n)
    (set! (b-closed b) (Cons (bb-slot cur) (deref (b-closed b))))
    (set! (b-closed-count b) (+ n 1))))

; Closing whichever block was open and moving on always lands on a
; block with no terminator yet (even if the block we're leaving had
; one) — clearing `terminated` here, unconditionally, is what lets
; `block-terminated?` answer for "the block open right now", not "the
; block open when some earlier value was produced".
(defn switch-to! (b: Builder) (target: BB) -> Unit
  (do
    (close-current! b)
    (set! (b-cur b) target)
    (set! (b-terminated b) false)))

; The one open block left when the function's body is fully lowered
; (`main`'s or an ordinary function's final `ret`'s own block) never
; goes through `switch-to!`; this closes it explicitly, exactly once,
; right before `total-blocks`/`builder-items-ordered` read the result.
(defn finish-builder! (b: Builder) -> Unit (close-current! b))

(defn total-blocks (b: Builder) -> Int (deref (b-closed-count b)))

(defn pending-reverse-onto (xs: (List PendingItem)) (acc: (List PendingItem)) -> (List PendingItem)
  (match xs [] acc (Cons x rest) (pending-reverse-onto rest (Cons x acc))))

(defn blocks-reverse-onto (xs: (List (Ref (List PendingItem)))) (acc: (List (Ref (List PendingItem)))) -> (List (Ref (List PendingItem)))
  (match xs [] acc (Cons x rest) (blocks-reverse-onto rest (Cons x acc))))

(defn append-items (xs: (List Item)) (ys: (List Item)) -> (List Item)
  (match xs [] ys (Cons x rest) (Cons x (append-items rest ys))))

; Every block's own `idx-ref` is resolved by now (`finish-builder!` has
; already run) — a `PBr`/`PCondBr`'s target(s) can finally be read.
(defn resolve-pending (p: PendingItem) -> Item
  (match p
    (PDone it) it
    (PBr r) (IBr (deref r))
    (PCondBr t f c) (ICondBr (deref t) (deref f) c)))

(defn resolve-pending-list (xs: (List PendingItem)) -> (List Item)
  (match xs [] [] (Cons x rest) (Cons (resolve-pending x) (resolve-pending-list rest))))

; `closed` accumulated blocks in closure order via Cons-prepend, so one
; reversal recovers that order; each block's own content was likewise
; Cons-prepended by `emit-pending!`, needing the same one-time reversal
; before its `PendingItem`s can be resolved and concatenated into the
; final flat stream `write-module-bc` expects.
(defn flatten-blocks (ordered: (List (Ref (List PendingItem)))) -> (List Item)
  (match ordered
    [] []
    (Cons slot rest) (append-items (resolve-pending-list (pending-reverse-onto (deref slot) [])) (flatten-blocks rest))))

(defn builder-items-ordered (b: Builder) -> (List Item)
  (flatten-blocks (blocks-reverse-onto (deref (b-closed b)) [])))

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Builder operations — each one appends exactly the `Item`(s) its name
; says, computing every relative reference at the moment of appending
; (see header comment's "`next-val` ... at the moment an instruction is
; appended"), and returns the fresh value's absolute id where it produces
; one.

; See header comment's "Constants are never cached across a function" —
; every call here is a brand-new `Item`, deliberately never deduped.
(defn const-i64! (b: Builder) (raw: Int) -> Int
  (do (emit! b (IConstI64 (encode-signed-i64 raw))) (bump-val! b)))

(defn const-i32! (b: Builder) (raw: Int) -> Int
  (do (emit! b (IConstI32 (encode-signed-i64 raw))) (bump-val! b)))

; `t(v) = (v << 1) | 1` — the raw i64 value a tagged `Int` literal `v`
; is; `const-i64!` then encodes *that* per the bitcode's own zig-zag
; integer-constant scheme (two independent layers — see `bc-writer.mnd`'s
; `encode-signed-i64` doc comment).
(defn const-tagged! (b: Builder) (v: Int) -> Int
  (const-i64! b (+ (* v 2) 1)))

; Bool/Unit immediates (slice 3B): false/Unit = 1, true = 3.
(defn const-false! (b: Builder) -> Int (const-i64! b 1))
(defn const-true! (b: Builder) -> Int (const-i64! b 3))
(defn const-unit! (b: Builder) -> Int (const-i64! b 1))
(defn const-bool! (b: Builder) (v: Bool) -> Int
  (if v (const-true! b) (const-false! b)))

; `i1` from icmp → Bool immediate: zext to i64 (0/1) then retag → 1/3.
(defn bool-from-i1! (b: Builder) (cond-abs: Int) -> Int
  (do
    (let z (emit-cast! b cast-zext cond-abs ty-i64))
    (arith-retag! b z)))

(defn emit-binop! (b: Builder) (op: Int) (lhs-abs: Int) (rhs-abs: Int) -> Int
  (do
    (let it (IBinop op (rel-ref b lhs-abs) (rel-ref b rhs-abs)))
    (emit! b it)
    (bump-val! b)))

(defn emit-cmp2! (b: Builder) (pred: Int) (lhs-abs: Int) (rhs-abs: Int) -> Int
  (do
    (let it (ICmp2 pred (rel-ref b lhs-abs) (rel-ref b rhs-abs)))
    (emit! b it)
    (bump-val! b)))

(defn emit-cast! (b: Builder) (op: Int) (val-abs: Int) (to-ty: Int) -> Int
  (do
    (let it (ICast op (rel-ref b val-abs) to-ty))
    (emit! b it)
    (bump-val! b)))

; `alloca i64, align 8`. The array-size operand is a fresh `i32` `1`
; (never cached — see above); its id is absolute, not relative, per
; `llvm-ir.mnd`'s `IAlloca` doc comment.
(defn emit-alloca! (b: Builder) -> Int
  (do
    (let size-abs (const-i32! b 1))
    (emit! b (IAlloca size-abs))
    (bump-val! b)))

(defn emit-store! (b: Builder) (ptr-abs: Int) (val-abs: Int) -> Unit
  (emit! b (IStore (rel-ref b ptr-abs) (rel-ref b val-abs))))

(defn emit-load! (b: Builder) (ptr-abs: Int) -> Int
  (do (emit! b (ILoad (rel-ref b ptr-abs))) (bump-val! b)))

; Branch targets are `BB` handles, not raw ints — their real index is
; unresolved until closure (see header comment); `emit-pending!` files
; a `PBr`/`PCondBr` carrying the target's own `idx-ref` directly, to be
; read back only once every block has closed.
(defn emit-br! (b: Builder) (target: BB) -> Unit
  (do
    (emit-pending! b (PBr (bb-idx-ref target)))
    (mark-terminated! b)))

(defn emit-condbr! (b: Builder) (true-bb: BB) (false-bb: BB) (cond-abs: Int) -> Unit
  (do
    (emit-pending! b (PCondBr (bb-idx-ref true-bb) (bb-idx-ref false-bb) (rel-ref b cond-abs)))
    (mark-terminated! b)))

(defn rel-refs (b: Builder) (xs: (List Int)) -> (List Int)
  (match xs [] [] (Cons x rest) (Cons (rel-ref b x) (rel-refs b rest))))

(defn emit-call! (b: Builder) (callee-abs: Int) (arg-abs: (List Int)) -> Int
  (do
    (let callee-rel (rel-ref b callee-abs))
    (let arg-rels (rel-refs b arg-abs))
    (emit! b (ICall callee-rel arg-rels))
    (bump-val! b)))

; May-collect functions keep every Menard word in a shadow slot and reload
; it at each use, so a copying collection can update the slot. The index
; `mn_root_keep` returns is a tagged immediate, not a pointer.
(defn is-rooting (b: Builder) -> Bool (deref (b-rooting b)))

(defn keep! (b: Builder) (v: Int) -> Int
  (if (or (not (is-rooting b)) (block-terminated? b)) v
    (emit-call! b (extern-root-keep-abs (deref (b-root-ns b))) [v])))

(defn get! (b: Builder) (v: Int) -> Int
  (if (or (not (is-rooting b)) (block-terminated? b)) v
    (emit-call! b (extern-root-get-abs (deref (b-root-ns b))) [v])))

(defn get-words! (b: Builder) (xs: (List Int)) -> (List Int)
  (match xs
    [] []
    (Cons x rest) (Cons (get! b x) (get-words! b rest))))

(defn emit-call-words! (b: Builder) (callee-abs: Int) (arg-abs: (List Int)) -> Int
  (emit-call! b callee-abs (get-words! b arg-abs)))

(defn emit-root-save! (b: Builder) -> Int
  (emit-call! b (extern-root-save-abs (deref (b-root-ns b))) []))

(defn emit-root-restore! (b: Builder) (depth-abs: Int) -> Unit
  (if (is-rooting b)
    (do
      (emit-call! b (extern-root-restore-abs (deref (b-root-ns b))) [depth-abs])
      ())
    ()))

; Alloca whose address is on the shadow stack. The push is a real
; `ptr` call so LLVM cannot drop the following store or fold the slot
; into an incoming stack argument (which the push would then zero).
; Allocation-free functions get a plain alloca.
(defn root-alloca! (b: Builder) -> Int
  (let slot (emit-alloca! b))
  (if (is-rooting b)
    (do
      (emit-call-void! b extern-kind-write (extern-root-push-abs (deref (b-root-ns b)))
        [slot (const-i64! b 0)])
      slot)
    slot))

(defn emit-ret! (b: Builder) (val-abs: Int) -> Unit
  (do
    (emit! b (IRet (rel-ref b val-abs)))
    (mark-terminated! b)))

(defn emit-unreachable! (b: Builder) -> Unit
  (do
    (emit! b (IUnreachable))
    (mark-terminated! b)))

; `if`'s (and `loop`'s) own "does this branch's value even reach the
; join/exit block" check — see `LoopFrame`'s doc comment. If the block
; open right now already ended in a terminator (a `recur` branching
; straight back to its loop's header, several `if`/`loop` levels down),
; a further `store`+`br` here would be a second terminator in the same
; block — always wrong, never merely redundant — so this is skipped
; entirely; the caller's `switch-to!` to whatever comes next still runs
; unconditionally, exactly as if this branch had produced a value.
(defn maybe-store-and-br! (b: Builder) (result-slot: Int) (val-abs: Int) (target: BB) -> Unit
  (if (block-terminated? b) ()
    ; The slot holds a root index (an immediate). The join reloads it
    ; with `get!`. Storing the index, not the word, means this alloca
    ; does not have to be a shadow root — including when the `if` sits
    ; in a loop header.
    (do (emit-store! b result-slot val-abs) (emit-br! b target))))

; `+`/`-`: free plus a one-instruction fixup (header comment's "The
; tagged-`Int` ABI, literally").
(defn arith-add! (b: Builder) (av: Int) (cv: Int) -> Int
  (do
    (let sum (emit-binop! b binop-add av cv))
    (let one (const-i64! b 1))
    (emit-binop! b binop-sub sum one)))

(defn arith-sub! (b: Builder) (av: Int) (cv: Int) -> Int
  (do
    (let diff (emit-binop! b binop-sub av cv))
    (let one (const-i64! b 1))
    (emit-binop! b binop-add diff one)))

; untag (`ashr 1`) / retag (`shl 1`, `or 1`) — shared by `*`/`/`/`%`.
(defn arith-untag! (b: Builder) (v: Int) -> Int
  (do
    (let one (const-i64! b 1))
    (emit-binop! b binop-ashr v one)))

(defn arith-retag! (b: Builder) (v: Int) -> Int
  (do
    (let one (const-i64! b 1))
    (let shifted (emit-binop! b binop-shl v one))
    (emit-binop! b binop-or shifted one)))

(defn arith-mul! (b: Builder) (av: Int) (cv: Int) -> Int
  (do
    (let ua (arith-untag! b av))
    (let uc (arith-untag! b cv))
    (let prod (emit-binop! b binop-mul ua uc))
    (arith-retag! b prod)))

; A zero divisor panics before `sdiv`/`srem`. The panic block does not
; fall through: `mn_panic` does not return, and `unreachable` is the
; terminator. The success block stays open so the retagged result is
; the value later instructions see.
; `file-gid` is the NUL-terminated path global. `line` is a raw i64, not a tagged Int.
(defn arith-checked! (b: Builder) (panic-at-abs: Int) (file-gid: Int) (line: Int) (msg-gid: Int) (op: Int) (av: Int) (cv: Int) -> Int
  (do
    (let ua (arith-untag! b av))
    (let uc (arith-untag! b cv))
    (let zero (const-i64! b 0))
    (let is-zero (emit-cmp2! b icmp-eq uc zero))
    (let panic-bb (fresh-bb! b))
    (let ok-bb (fresh-bb! b))
    (emit-condbr! b panic-bb ok-bb is-zero)
    (switch-to! b panic-bb)
    (let line-c (const-i64! b line))
    (emit-call-void! b extern-kind-panic-at panic-at-abs [file-gid line-c msg-gid])
    (emit-unreachable! b)
    (switch-to! b ok-bb)
    (arith-retag! b (emit-binop! b op ua uc))))

(defn arith-div! (b: Builder) (panic-at-abs: Int) (file-gid: Int) (line: Int) (msg-gid: Int) (av: Int) (cv: Int) -> Int
  (arith-checked! b panic-at-abs file-gid line msg-gid binop-sdiv av cv))

(defn arith-rem! (b: Builder) (panic-at-abs: Int) (file-gid: Int) (line: Int) (msg-gid: Int) (av: Int) (cv: Int) -> Int
  (arith-checked! b panic-at-abs file-gid line msg-gid binop-srem av cv))

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; `StrPool` — every distinct `Str` literal `println`/`print`/`write`
; lowering needs a global for, deduped by content (so two `(println
; "x")` call sites, or a `println` and an unrelated `(write 1 "x")` that
; happen to share literal text, share one global rather than each
; getting their own — see `newline-str`'s own doc comment for why this
; matters even for a program with only one distinct user-visible
; string). Two passes share this one type:
;
; 1. **Collection** (`collect-str-pool`, called once by `lower-program`,
;    before lowering anything): a pure syntactic walk of *every* form —
;    every top-level form and every `defn`'s body, recursing into every
;    nested `ParenNode`/`BracketNode` unconditionally — looking for a
;    `println`/`print`/`write` call shape and pulling out its `Str`-
;    literal argument(s) (`println` additionally, always, adds
;    `newline-str` — even a bare `(println)`). This never calls
;    `lower-expr` and needs no `env`/`funcs`/`noop`: it is *purely*
;    syntactic, so it cannot fail, and — critically — it can run before
;    `num-globals` (how many ids every function's own local `Builder`
;    numbering must start after, see `lower-program-build`) is known,
;    which real lowering's own value ids depend on.
; 2. **Lookup** (`str-pool-get`, called throughout real lowering): the
;    *same* pool, finalized (`str-pool-finalize`, which fixes the three
;    runtike externs' own abs ids once the final string count is known
;    — see `llvm-ir.mnd`'s `extern-write-stdout-abs`/etc.), threaded
;    through every `lower-*` function (the same way `funcs`/`noop`
;    already are) purely so `println`/`print`/`write`'s own lowering can
;    look up which abs id a given literal's global occupies — by
;    *content*, not by traversal order, so collection and lowering never
;    need to visit nodes in lock-step for this to stay correct.
;
; `order-rev` accumulates in reverse (`Cons`-prepend, same rationale as
; `Builder`'s own `items`); `str-pool-strs` reverses it once, for
; `LlvmModule`'s `globals` (id `0..S-1`, in `pool.mnd`'s sorted order,
; with `println`'s newline appended when it is not already a literal).
(pub defrec CtorSpec (tag: Int) (arity: Int))
(defn ctor-spec-tag (c: CtorSpec) -> Int (match c (CtorSpec t _) t))
(defn ctor-spec-arity (c: CtorSpec) -> Int (match c (CtorSpec _ a) a))

(defrec StrPool (order-rev: (List Str)) (by-content: (Map Str Int)) (next: Int) (write-stdout-abs: Int) (print-i64-abs: Int) (write-stderr-abs: Int) (ctors: (Map Str CtorSpec)) (origins: (List Str)) (file-gids: (Ref (Map Str Int))))

(defn str-pool-order-rev (p: StrPool) -> (List Str) (match p (StrPool o _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _) o))
(defn str-pool-by-content (p: StrPool) -> (Map Str Int) (match p (StrPool _ m _ _ _ _ _ _ _) m))
(defn str-pool-next (p: StrPool) -> Int (match p (StrPool _ _ n _ _ _ _ _ _) n))
(defn str-pool-write-stdout-abs (p: StrPool) -> Int (match p (StrPool _ _ _ w _ _ _ _ _) w))
(defn str-pool-print-i64-abs (p: StrPool) -> Int (match p (StrPool _ _ _ _ pr _ _ _ _) pr))
(defn str-pool-write-stderr-abs (p: StrPool) -> Int (match p (StrPool _ _ _ _ _ e _ _ _) e))
(defn str-pool-ctors (p: StrPool) -> (Map Str CtorSpec) (match p (StrPool _ _ _ _ _ _ c _ _) c))
(defn str-pool-origins (p: StrPool) -> (List Str) (match p (StrPool _ _ _ _ _ _ _ o _) o))
(defn str-pool-file-gids (p: StrPool) -> (Ref (Map Str Int)) (match p (StrPool _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ g) g))

; Every abs-id field is meaningless until `str-pool-finalize` runs
; (collection alone never reads them) — `0 - 1` (`-1`) as a visibly
; invalid placeholder, same convention `new-bb`'s unresolved index uses.
(defn str-pool-new (origins: (List Str)) -> StrPool
  (StrPool [] (map-new) 0 (- 1) (- 1) (- 1) (map-new) origins (ref (map-new))))

(defn str-pool-count (p: StrPool) -> Int (str-pool-next p))

(defn str-pool-add (p: StrPool) (s: Str) -> StrPool
  (match (map-get (str-pool-by-content p) s)
    (Some _) p
    (None) (StrPool
      (Cons s (str-pool-order-rev p))
      (map-set (str-pool-by-content p) s (str-pool-next p))
      (+ (str-pool-next p) 1)
      (str-pool-write-stdout-abs p)
      (str-pool-print-i64-abs p)
      (str-pool-write-stderr-abs p)
      (str-pool-ctors p)
      (str-pool-origins p)
      (str-pool-file-gids p))))

; Always found once `str-pool-add` has run over every occurrence
; `collect-str-pool` sees — see that function's header comment for why
; this content-keyed lookup never depends on traversal order matching.
(defn str-pool-get (p: StrPool) (s: Str) -> Int
  (match (map-get (str-pool-by-content p) s) (Some id) id (None) (- 1)))

(defn str-pool-strs (p: StrPool) -> (List Str) (reverse (str-pool-order-rev p)))

; Fixes the three externs' abs ids (`llvm-ir.mnd`'s `extern-write-stdout-
; abs`/etc.) once the final string count is known — called exactly once,
; by `lower-program-build`, right after collection finishes and before
; any real lowering begins. Also attaches the program's user-ctor table.
(defn str-pool-finalize (p: StrPool) (ctors: (Map Str CtorSpec)) -> StrPool
  (do
    (let s (str-pool-count p))
    (StrPool (str-pool-order-rev p) (str-pool-by-content p) (str-pool-next p) s (+ s 1) (+ s 2) ctors (str-pool-origins p) (str-pool-file-gids p))))

; String globals come from `pool.mnd`'s sorted literals. `newline-str` is
; appended so a bare `(println)` still has a global; `str-pool-add` leaves
; an existing literal where the sort put it.
(defn str-pool-from-list (xs: (List Str)) (p: StrPool) -> StrPool
  (match xs
    [] p
    (Cons s rest) (str-pool-from-list rest (str-pool-add p s))))

(defn list-nth-str (xs: (List Str)) (i: Int) -> Str
  (match xs
    [] ""
    (Cons h t) (if (<= i 0) h (list-nth-str t (- i 1)))))

(defn origin-path (pool: StrPool) (origin: Int) -> Str
  (list-nth-str (str-pool-origins pool) origin))

(defn c-str (s: Str) -> Str
  (do
    (let sb (sb-new))
    (sb-append! sb s)
    (sb-append-byte! sb 0)
    (sb-take-str! sb)))

(defn add-origin-cstrs (ps: (List Str)) (p: StrPool) -> StrPool
  (match ps
    [] (str-pool-add p (c-str ""))
    (Cons s rest) (add-origin-cstrs rest (str-pool-add p (c-str s)))))

(defn span-line-clamped (sp: Span) -> Int
  (do
    (let n (span-line sp))
    (if (< n 1) 1 n)))

(defn file-gid-of (pool: StrPool) (origin: Int) -> Int
  (do
    (let path (origin-path pool origin))
    (let gids (str-pool-file-gids pool))
    (match (map-get (deref gids) path)
      (Some id) id
      (None)
        (do
          (let id (str-pool-get pool (c-str path)))
          (set! gids (map-set (deref gids) path id))
          id))))

(defn collect-str-pool (forms: (List Ast)) (paths: (List Str)) -> StrPool
  (add-origin-cstrs paths
    (str-pool-add (str-pool-add (str-pool-from-list (pool-string-literals forms) (str-pool-new paths)) (newline-str)) (div-zero-msg))))

; -- real lowering's own void-call emission: `println`/`print`/`write`
; call one of the three fixed runtime externs directly (never a real
; user-defined `defn`), producing no `Int` value at all (spec: `Unit`) —
; see `llvm-ir.mnd`'s `ICallVoid` doc comment for why this needs its own
; `Item`/emission path rather than reusing `emit-call!`, which always
; assumes (and bumps a value id for) an `Int`-returning callee. --

(defn emit-call-void! (b: Builder) (kind: Int) (callee-abs: Int) (arg-abs: (List Int)) -> Unit
  (do
    (let callee-rel (rel-ref b callee-abs))
    (let arg-rels (rel-refs b arg-abs))
    (emit! b (ICallVoid kind callee-rel arg-rels))))

; `mn_write_stdout`/`mn_write_stderr(ptr, i64)` — `s`'s own global
; (looked up by content in `pool`) and its byte length, a fresh `i64`
; constant (never cached — same rationale as every other constant in
; this module, see the header comment's "Constants are never cached").
(defn emit-write-str-to! (b: Builder) (pool: StrPool) (s: Str) (callee-abs: Int) -> Unit
  (do
    (let gid (str-pool-get pool s))
    (let len-abs (const-i64! b (str-byte-length s)))
    (emit-call-void! b extern-kind-write callee-abs [gid len-abs])))

; `mn_print_i64(i64)` — `v`'s already-tagged `Int` value, untagged
; (`arith-untag!`, the same `ashr 1` `*`/`/`/`%` already share) before
; the call: the runtime helper takes a plain machine `int64_t`, per its
; own doc comment (`runtime/include/menard.h`).
(defn emit-print-i64! (b: Builder) (pool: StrPool) (v: Int) -> Unit
  (do
    (let untagged (arith-untag! b (get! b v)))
    (emit-call-void! b extern-kind-print (str-pool-print-i64-abs pool) [untagged])))

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; The lowerer proper. `env` binds a body's local names (params, `let`s)
; to alloca absolute ids; `funcs` is every lowerable (`Int`-only) `defn`,
; for calls; `noop` is every `Unit`, zero-arg, empty-body `defn`'s name,
; for the shadow-push/pop skip (see header comment).

(defn is-arith-binop (s: Str) -> Bool
  (or (= s "+") (= s "-") (= s "*") (= s "/") (= s "%")))

(defn is-cmp-op (s: Str) -> Bool
  (or (= s "<") (= s ">") (= s "<=") (= s ">=") (= s "=")))

(defn str-in-list (s: Str) (xs: (List Str)) -> Bool
  (match xs
    [] false
    (Cons x rest) (if (= s x) true (str-in-list s rest))))

(defn unsupported-form-names -> (List Str)
  ["quote"])

(defn is-unsupported-form (s: Str) -> Bool
  (str-in-list s (unsupported-form-names)))

(defn lower-expr (ast: Ast) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (result-bind (lower-expr-raw ast env b funcs noop pool) (fn (v) (Ok (keep! b v)))))

(defn lower-expr-raw (ast: Ast) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (match ast
    (IntNode n _) (Ok (const-tagged! b n))
    (BoolNode v _) (Ok (const-bool! b v))
    (SymNode name _) (lower-sym name env b funcs pool)
    (ParenNode elems sp) (lower-paren elems sp env b funcs noop pool)
    (BracketNode _ _) (Err "cannot lower a list literal with the real instruction lowerer yet")
    (StrNode s _) (Ok (emit-str-lit! b pool s))
    (FloatNode s _) (Ok (emit-float-lit! b pool s))))

(defn emit-float-lit! (b: Builder) (pool: StrPool) (s: Str) -> Int
  (do
    (let gid (str-pool-get pool s))
    (let ptr-i64 (emit-cast! b cast-ptrtoint gid ty-i64))
    (let len (const-i64! b (str-byte-length s)))
    (emit-call! b (extern-float-from-str-abs (str-pool-count pool)) [ptr-i64 len])))

(defn emit-str-lit! (b: Builder) (pool: StrPool) (s: Str) -> Int
  (do
    (let gid (str-pool-get pool s))
    (let ptr-i64 (emit-cast! b cast-ptrtoint gid ty-i64))
    (let len (const-i64! b (str-byte-length s)))
    (emit-call! b (extern-str-new-abs (str-pool-count pool)) [ptr-i64 len])))

(defn lower-sym (name: Str) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (match (map-get env name)
    (Some slot) (Ok (emit-load! b slot))
    (None)
      (match (map-get funcs name)
        (Some fr) (lower-func-as-value fr b pool)
        (None) (lower-sym-ctor-or-err name b pool))))

(defn lower-func-as-value (fr: FuncRef) (b: Builder) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (do
    ; `func-ref-abs` is already the module-scope absolute id
    ; (`num-strings + extern-count + idx`).
    (let code (emit-cast! b cast-ptrtoint (func-ref-abs fr) ty-i64))
    (Ok (emit-call! b (extern-closure-bare-abs (str-pool-count pool)) [code]))))

(defn lower-sym-ctor-or-err (name: Str) (b: Builder) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (match (ctor-tag-of name pool)
    (None) (Err (str-concat "cannot lower unbound name " name))
    (Some tag)
      (do
        (let ns (str-pool-count pool))
        (let arity (ctor-arity-of name pool))
        (if (= arity 0)
          ; Nullary ctor as an expression *is* the value (Nil, None, …).
          (if (is-builtin-ctor name)
            (Ok (emit-call! b (ctor-extern-abs name ns) []))
            (do
              (let tag-c (const-i64! b tag))
              (let ar-c (const-i64! b 0))
              (Ok (emit-call! b (extern-new-abs ns) [tag-c ar-c]))))
          (do
            (let tag-c (const-i64! b tag))
            (let ar-c (const-i64! b arity))
            (Ok (emit-call! b (extern-ctor-closure-abs ns) [tag-c ar-c])))))))

; A reader span covers a source extent (`end` > `start`). Compiler-built
; calls — the import bootstrap's calls to module inits and to the entry
; `main` — use a zero-width span (`graph.mnd`'s `dummy-span`). That span's
; origin is 0, the first loaded file, so recording it names the wrong file.
(defn span-located (sp: Span) -> Bool
  (> (span-end sp) (span-start sp)))

(defn emit-trace-push! (b: Builder) (pool: StrPool) (sp: Span) -> Unit
  (do
    (let file-gid (file-gid-of pool (span-origin sp)))
    (let line (const-i64! b (span-line-clamped sp)))
    (emit-call-void! b extern-kind-trace-push (extern-trace-push-abs (str-pool-count pool)) [file-gid line])))

(defn emit-trace-pop! (b: Builder) (pool: StrPool) -> Unit
  (emit-call-void! b extern-kind-trace-pop (extern-trace-pop-abs (str-pool-count pool)) []))

; Push the call expression's file and line, call, then pop. A panic inside
; the callee leaves the frame in place. A zero-width span is not a source
; location, so the call is emitted with no frame.
; `args` are the words the call should receive. Callers that still hold root
; indexes reload them first; this wrapper does not, so a value loaded out of
; a shadow slot is not passed to `mn_root_get` a second time.
(defn emit-traced-call-at! (b: Builder) (pool: StrPool) (sp: Span) (callee: Int) (args: (List Int)) -> Int
  (do
    (emit-trace-push! b pool sp)
    (let v (emit-call! b callee args))
    (emit-trace-pop! b pool)
    v))

(defn emit-traced-call! (b: Builder) (pool: StrPool) (sp: Span) (callee: Int) (args: (List Int)) -> Int
  (if (span-located sp)
    (emit-traced-call-at! b pool sp callee args)
    (emit-call! b callee args)))

(defn lower-paren (elems: (List Ast)) (sp: Span) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (match elems
    [] (Ok (const-unit! b))
    (Cons head rest) (lower-paren-head head rest sp env b funcs noop pool)))

(defn lower-paren-head (head: Ast) (rest: (List Ast)) (sp: Span) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (match (sym-str head)
    (None) (lower-apply-value head rest sp env b funcs noop pool)
    (Some hn) (lower-named hn rest sp env b funcs noop pool)))

(defn lower-apply-value (head: Ast) (args: (List Ast)) (sp: Span) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (result-bind (lower-expr head env b funcs noop pool)
    (fn (clo) (lower-apply-clo clo args sp env b funcs noop pool))))

(defn lower-apply-clo (clo: Int) (args: (List Ast)) (sp: Span) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (match args
    [] (Ok (emit-traced-call! b pool sp (extern-apply-0-abs (str-pool-count pool)) (get-words! b [clo])))
    [a0]
      (result-bind (lower-expr a0 env b funcs noop pool)
        (fn (arg) (Ok (emit-traced-call! b pool sp (extern-apply-1-abs (str-pool-count pool)) (get-words! b [clo arg])))))
    [a0 a1]
      (result-bind (lower-expr a0 env b funcs noop pool)
        (fn (x) (result-bind (lower-expr a1 env b funcs noop pool)
          (fn (y) (Ok (emit-traced-call! b pool sp (extern-apply-2-abs (str-pool-count pool)) (get-words! b [clo x y])))))))
    _ (Err "closure application supports at most 2 arguments currently")))

(defn lower-named (hn: Str) (rest: (List Ast)) (sp: Span) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (if (= hn "if") (lower-if rest env b funcs noop pool)
    (if (= hn "let") (lower-let-inline rest env b funcs noop pool)
      (if (= hn "do") (lower-sequence rest env b funcs noop pool)
        (if (= hn "loop") (lower-loop rest env b funcs noop pool)
          (if (= hn "recur") (lower-recur rest env b funcs noop pool)
            (if (= hn "match") (lower-match rest env b funcs noop pool)
              (if (is-arith-binop hn) (lower-arith rest hn sp env b funcs noop pool)
                (if (is-cmp-op hn) (lower-cmp-value rest hn env b funcs noop pool)
                  (if (is-ctor-name hn pool) (lower-ctor hn rest env b funcs noop pool)
                    (match (map-get funcs hn)
                      (Some _) (lower-call hn rest sp env b funcs noop pool)
                      (None)
                        (if (is-runtime-op hn) (lower-runtime-op hn rest env b funcs noop pool)
                          (if (is-effect-head hn)
                            (result-then (lower-effect-op hn rest env b funcs noop pool) (fn () (Ok (const-unit! b))))
                            (if (is-unsupported-form hn) (Err (str-concat "cannot lower `" hn "` with the real instruction lowerer yet"))
                              (lower-call hn rest sp env b funcs noop pool)))))))))))))))

; -- if --

(defn lower-if (rest: (List Ast)) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (match rest
    [test then els]
      (result-bind (lower-cond test env b funcs noop pool) (fn (cond-abs) (lower-if-branches cond-abs then els env b funcs noop pool)))
    _ (Err "if requires a test, a then-branch and an else-branch")))

(defn lower-if-branches (cond-abs: Int) (then: Ast) (els: Ast) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (do
    ; `result-slot` is allocated into the block still open when the
    ; `if` is encountered — the one block guaranteed to dominate
    ; `then`, `else` and `join` alike, however many blocks each of
    ; those turns out to need internally (see `Builder`'s header
    ; comment).
    (let result-slot (emit-alloca! b))
    (let then-bb (fresh-bb! b))
    (let else-bb (fresh-bb! b))
    (let join-bb (fresh-bb! b))
    (emit-condbr! b then-bb else-bb cond-abs)
    (switch-to! b then-bb)
    (result-bind (lower-expr then env b funcs noop pool)
      (fn (then-val) (lower-if-then-done then-val els result-slot else-bb join-bb env b funcs noop pool)))))

(defn lower-if-then-done (then-val: Int) (els: Ast) (result-slot: Int) (else-bb: BB) (join-bb: BB) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (do
    ; `maybe-store-and-br!`: if `then` ended in `recur` (block already
    ; terminated), skip the store+br — a second terminator would be
    ; illegal. Still switch into `else` either way.
    (maybe-store-and-br! b result-slot then-val join-bb)
    (switch-to! b else-bb)
    (result-bind (lower-expr els env b funcs noop pool)
      (fn (else-val) (lower-if-else-done else-val result-slot join-bb b)))))

(defn lower-if-else-done (else-val: Int) (result-slot: Int) (join-bb: BB) (b: Builder) -> (Result Int Str)
  (do
    (maybe-store-and-br! b result-slot else-val join-bb)
    (switch-to! b join-bb)
    (Ok (get! b (emit-load! b result-slot)))))

; -- loop / recur (slice 3A) --
;
; `(loop ((name init)…) body)`: allocas for each binding + a result
; slot in the dominating block; store inits; br header; in header,
; lower body with names bound to those slots; a normal body value
; stores into the result slot and br's exit; `recur` stores new values
; and br's header. Nested loops push/pop `LoopFrame` on the Builder.

(defn binding-pair-of (ast: Ast) -> (Maybe (List Ast))
  (match ast
    (ParenNode [name-ast init-ast] _) (Some [name-ast init-ast])
    (BracketNode [name-ast init-ast] _) (Some [name-ast init-ast])
    _ (None)))

(defn binding-list-elems (ast: Ast) -> (Maybe (List Ast))
  (match ast
    (ParenNode elems _) (Some elems)
    (BracketNode elems _) (Some elems)
    _ (None)))

(defn lower-loop (rest: (List Ast)) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (match rest
    [bindings-ast body]
      (match (binding-list-elems bindings-ast)
        (None) (Err "loop bindings must be a list of (name init) pairs")
        (Some pairs) (lower-loop-with-pairs pairs body env b funcs noop pool))
    _ (Err "loop requires bindings and a body")))

(defn list-reverse-str (xs: (List Str)) -> (List Str)
  (list-reverse-str-onto xs []))
(defn list-reverse-str-onto (xs: (List Str)) (acc: (List Str)) -> (List Str)
  (match xs [] acc (Cons x rest) (list-reverse-str-onto rest (Cons x acc))))
(defn list-reverse-int (xs: (List Int)) -> (List Int)
  (list-reverse-int-onto xs []))
(defn list-reverse-int-onto (xs: (List Int)) (acc: (List Int)) -> (List Int)
  (match xs [] acc (Cons x rest) (list-reverse-int-onto rest (Cons x acc))))

(defn lower-loop-with-pairs (pairs: (List Ast)) (body: Ast) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (do
    (let result-slot (emit-alloca! b))
    (lower-loop-bind-all pairs body result-slot env b funcs noop pool [] [] env)))

(defn lower-loop-bind-all (pairs: (List Ast)) (body: Ast) (result-slot: Int) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) (names-acc: (List Str)) (slots-acc: (List Int)) (env-acc: (Map Str Int)) -> (Result Int Str)
  (match pairs
    [] (lower-loop-run body result-slot (list-reverse-str names-acc) (list-reverse-int slots-acc) env-acc b funcs noop pool)
    (Cons pair rest)
      (match (binding-pair-of pair)
        (None) (Err "each loop binding must be (name init)")
        (Some [name-ast init-ast])
          (match (sym-str name-ast)
            (None) (Err "loop binding name must be a symbol")
            (Some name)
              (result-bind (lower-expr init-ast env b funcs noop pool)
                (fn (v)
                  (do
                    (let slot (root-alloca! b))
                    (emit-store! b slot (get! b v))
                    (lower-loop-bind-all rest body result-slot env b funcs noop pool
                      (Cons name names-acc) (Cons slot slots-acc) (map-set env-acc name slot))))))
        _ (Err "each loop binding must be (name init)"))))

(defn lower-loop-run (body: Ast) (result-slot: Int) (names: (List Str)) (slots: (List Int)) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (do
    (let header (fresh-bb! b))
    (let exit-bb (fresh-bb! b))
    ; Save once, in the block that dominates the header, so `recur` can
    ; pop body roots without popping the loop slots rooted above.
    (let mark (if (is-rooting b) (emit-root-save! b) 0))
    (emit-br! b header)
    (switch-to! b header)
    (push-loop-frame! b (LoopFrame header exit-bb result-slot slots names mark))
    (result-bind (lower-expr body env b funcs noop pool)
      (fn (body-val)
        (do
          (maybe-store-and-br! b result-slot body-val exit-bb)
          (pop-loop-frame! b)
          (switch-to! b exit-bb)
          (Ok (get! b (emit-load! b result-slot))))))))

(defn lower-recur (rest: (List Ast)) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (match (current-loop-frame b)
    (None) (Err "recur outside loop")
    (Some lf) (lower-recur-eval-all rest [] (loop-frame-slots lf) (loop-frame-header lf) env b funcs noop pool)))

; Evaluate every `recur` argument *before* any store — parallel assignment
; (spec: all new bindings computed from the previous iteration's values).
; Storing as we go would make `(recur (+ i 1) (+ acc i))` see the updated
; `i` in the second argument.
(defn lower-recur-eval-all (args: (List Ast)) (vals-acc: (List Int)) (slots: (List Int)) (header: BB) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (match args
    [] (lower-recur-store-all (list-reverse-int vals-acc) slots header b)
    (Cons a rest)
      (result-bind (lower-expr a env b funcs noop pool)
        (fn (v) (lower-recur-eval-all rest (Cons v vals-acc) slots header env b funcs noop pool)))))

(defn lower-recur-store-all (vals: (List Int)) (slots: (List Int)) (header: BB) (b: Builder) -> (Result Int Str)
  (match vals
    []
      (match slots
        []
          (do
            (match (current-loop-frame b)
              (Some lf) (emit-root-restore! b (loop-frame-root-mark lf))
              (None) ())
            (emit-br! b header)
            (Ok (const-tagged! b 0)))
        _ (Err "recur argument count does not match loop bindings"))
    (Cons v rest-vals)
      (match slots
        [] (Err "recur argument count does not match loop bindings")
        (Cons slot rest-slots)
          (do
            (emit-store! b slot (get! b v))
            (lower-recur-store-all rest-vals rest-slots header b)))))

; -- builtin + user constructors + match (slice 3C / H) --

; User-ctor tags start here so they never collide with runtime tags
; (List/Maybe/Result 0–5, Str/Ref/SB 10–12, Map/IoError 20–27, closure 100+).
(let user-ctor-tag-base 1000)

(defn decl-name-of (name-part: Ast) -> (Maybe Str)
  (match name-part
    (SymNode n _) (Some n)
    (ParenNode (Cons n-ast _) _) (sym-str n-ast)
    _ (None)))

(defn register-ctor-spec (acc: (Map Str CtorSpec)) (name: Str) (arity: Int) (tag-ref: (Ref Int)) -> (Map Str CtorSpec)
  (do
    (let tag (deref tag-ref))
    (set! tag-ref (+ tag 1))
    (map-set acc name (CtorSpec tag arity))))

(defn register-one-variant-ctor (c: Ast) (acc: (Map Str CtorSpec)) (tag-ref: (Ref Int)) -> (Map Str CtorSpec)
  (match c
    (ParenNode (Cons cname-ast payload-asts) _)
      (match (sym-str cname-ast)
        (None) acc
        (Some cname) (register-variant-ctor-name cname payload-asts acc tag-ref))
    _ acc))

; IoError and SpawnStatus already have runtime tags (20–27, 30–31).
; Collecting them again would mint a user tag at 1000 and disagree with
; the objects the C functions return.
(defn register-variant-ctor-name (cname: Str) (payload-asts: (List Ast)) (acc: (Map Str CtorSpec)) (tag-ref: (Ref Int)) -> (Map Str CtorSpec)
  (match (builtin-ctor-tag-of cname)
    (Some _) acc
    (None) (register-ctor-spec acc cname (length payload-asts) tag-ref)))

(defn register-variant-ctors (ctors: (List Ast)) (acc: (Map Str CtorSpec)) (tag-ref: (Ref Int)) -> (Map Str CtorSpec)
  (match ctors
    [] acc
    (Cons c rest) (register-variant-ctors rest (register-one-variant-ctor c acc tag-ref) tag-ref)))

(defn collect-variant-decl (rest: (List Ast)) (acc: (Map Str CtorSpec)) (tag-ref: (Ref Int)) -> (Map Str CtorSpec)
  (match rest
    (Cons _name-part ctors) (register-variant-ctors ctors acc tag-ref)
    [] acc))

(defn collect-defrec-decl (rest: (List Ast)) (acc: (Map Str CtorSpec)) (tag-ref: (Ref Int)) -> (Map Str CtorSpec)
  (match rest
    (Cons name-part fields)
      (match (decl-name-of name-part)
        (None) acc
        (Some name)
          (match (builtin-ctor-tag-of name)
            (Some _) acc
            (None) (register-ctor-spec acc name (length fields) tag-ref)))
    [] acc))

(defn collect-ctors-named (hn: Str) (rest: (List Ast)) (acc: (Map Str CtorSpec)) (tag-ref: (Ref Int)) -> (Map Str CtorSpec)
  (if (= hn "variant") (collect-variant-decl rest acc tag-ref)
    (if (= hn "defrec") (collect-defrec-decl rest acc tag-ref)
      acc)))

(defn collect-ctors-form (ast: Ast) (acc: (Map Str CtorSpec)) (tag-ref: (Ref Int)) -> (Map Str CtorSpec)
  (match (unwrap-pub ast)
    (ParenNode (Cons head rest) _)
      (match (sym-str head)
        (None) acc
        (Some hn) (collect-ctors-named hn rest acc tag-ref))
    _ acc))

(defn collect-ctors-forms (forms: (List Ast)) (acc: (Map Str CtorSpec)) (tag-ref: (Ref Int)) -> (Map Str CtorSpec)
  (match forms
    [] acc
    (Cons f rest) (collect-ctors-forms rest (collect-ctors-form f acc tag-ref) tag-ref)))

(defn collect-user-ctors (forms: (List Ast)) -> (Map Str CtorSpec)
  (do
    (let tag-ref (ref user-ctor-tag-base))
    (collect-ctors-forms forms (map-new) tag-ref)))

(defn is-builtin-ctor (hn: Str) -> Bool
  (or (= hn "Nil") (= hn "Cons") (= hn "None") (= hn "Some") (= hn "Ok") (= hn "Err")))

(defn is-user-ctor (hn: Str) (pool: StrPool) -> Bool
  (match (map-get (str-pool-ctors pool) hn) (Some _) true (None) false))

(defn has-builtin-tag (hn: Str) -> Bool
  (match (builtin-ctor-tag-of hn)
    (Some _) true
    (None) false))

(defn is-ctor-name (hn: Str) (pool: StrPool) -> Bool
  (or (has-builtin-tag hn) (is-user-ctor hn pool)))

(defn builtin-ctor-tag-of (hn: Str) -> (Maybe Int)
  (if (= hn "Nil") (Some tag-nil)
    (if (= hn "Cons") (Some tag-cons)
      (if (= hn "None") (Some tag-none)
        (if (= hn "Some") (Some tag-some)
          (if (= hn "Ok") (Some tag-ok)
            (if (= hn "Err") (Some tag-err)
              ; IoError ctors — constructed by the runtime, matched in user code.
              (if (= hn "NotFound") (Some 20)
                (if (= hn "Permission") (Some 21)
                  (if (= hn "Exists") (Some 22)
                    (if (= hn "IsADirectory") (Some 23)
                      (if (= hn "NotADirectory") (Some 24)
                        (if (= hn "InvalidPath") (Some 25)
                          (if (= hn "TooLarge") (Some 26)
                            (if (= hn "Other") (Some 27)
                              (if (= hn "Exited") (Some 30)
                                (if (= hn "Signalled") (Some 31)
                                  (if (= hn "SpawnOutput") (Some 32)
                                    (if (= hn "NotExecutable") (Some 33)
                                      (if (= hn "InvalidArgument") (Some 34)
                                        (if (= hn "TooManyArguments") (Some 35)
                                          (if (= hn "Unsupported") (Some 36) (None)))))))))))))))))))))))

(defn ctor-tag-of (hn: Str) (pool: StrPool) -> (Maybe Int)
  (match (builtin-ctor-tag-of hn)
    (Some t) (Some t)
    (None)
      (match (map-get (str-pool-ctors pool) hn)
        (Some spec) (Some (ctor-spec-tag spec))
        (None) (None))))

(defn seam-fixed-arity (hn: Str) -> (Maybe Int)
  (if (= hn "SpawnOutput") (Some 3)
    (if (or (= hn "Other") (= hn "Exited") (= hn "Signalled")) (Some 1)
      (if (or (= hn "NotFound")
              (= hn "Permission")
              (= hn "Exists")
              (= hn "IsADirectory")
              (= hn "NotADirectory")
              (= hn "InvalidPath")
              (= hn "TooLarge")
              (= hn "NotExecutable")
              (= hn "InvalidArgument")
              (= hn "TooManyArguments")
              (= hn "Unsupported")) (Some 0)
        (None)))))

(defn ctor-arity-of (hn: Str) (pool: StrPool) -> Int
  (match (seam-fixed-arity hn)
    (Some n) n
    (None)
      (if (or (= hn "Nil") (= hn "None")) 0
        (if (= hn "Cons") 2
          (if (or (= hn "Some") (= hn "Ok") (= hn "Err")) 1
            (match (map-get (str-pool-ctors pool) hn)
              (Some spec) (ctor-spec-arity spec)
              (None) (- 1)))))))

(defn ctor-extern-abs (hn: Str) (ns: Int) -> Int
  (if (= hn "Nil") (extern-nil-abs ns)
    (if (= hn "Cons") (extern-cons-abs ns)
      (if (= hn "None") (extern-none-abs ns)
        (if (= hn "Some") (extern-some-abs ns)
          (if (= hn "Ok") (extern-ok-abs ns) (extern-err-abs ns)))))))

(defn lower-user-ctor-fill (obj: Int) (avs: (List Int)) (i: Int) (b: Builder) (pool: StrPool) -> Int
  (match avs
    [] obj
    (Cons v rest)
      (do
        (let idx (const-i64! b i))
        (let obj2 (emit-call! b (extern-set-slot-abs (str-pool-count pool)) [obj idx (get! b v)]))
        (lower-user-ctor-fill obj2 rest (+ i 1) b pool))))

(defn lower-user-ctor (hn: Str) (args: (List Ast)) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (match (map-get (str-pool-ctors pool) hn)
    (None) (Err (str-concat "unknown constructor " hn))
    (Some spec)
      (if (= (length args) (ctor-spec-arity spec))
        (result-bind (lower-args args env b funcs noop pool)
          (fn (avs)
            (do
              (let tag-c (const-i64! b (ctor-spec-tag spec)))
              (let nslots (const-i64! b (ctor-spec-arity spec)))
              (let obj (emit-call! b (extern-new-abs (str-pool-count pool)) [tag-c nslots]))
              (Ok (lower-user-ctor-fill obj avs 0 b pool)))))
        (Err (str-concat "arity mismatch constructing " hn)))))

(defn lower-fixed-tag-ctor (hn: Str) (args: (List Ast)) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (match (builtin-ctor-tag-of hn)
    (None) (Err (str-concat "unknown constructor " hn))
    (Some tag)
      (if (= (length args) (ctor-arity-of hn pool))
        (result-bind (lower-args args env b funcs noop pool)
          (fn (avs)
            (do
              (let tag-c (const-i64! b tag))
              (let nslots (const-i64! b (ctor-arity-of hn pool)))
              (let obj (emit-call! b (extern-new-abs (str-pool-count pool)) [tag-c nslots]))
              (Ok (lower-user-ctor-fill obj avs 0 b pool)))))
        (Err (str-concat "arity mismatch constructing " hn)))))

(defn lower-ctor (hn: Str) (args: (List Ast)) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (if (is-builtin-ctor hn)
    (if (= (length args) (ctor-arity-of hn pool))
      (result-bind (lower-args args env b funcs noop pool)
        (fn (avs) (Ok (emit-call-words! b (ctor-extern-abs hn (str-pool-count pool)) avs))))
      (Err (str-concat "arity mismatch constructing " hn)))
    (if (has-builtin-tag hn)
      (lower-fixed-tag-ctor hn args env b funcs noop pool)
      (lower-user-ctor hn args env b funcs noop pool))))

(defn is-runtime-op (hn: Str) -> Bool
  (str-in-list hn (runtime-op-names)))

(defn runtime-op-names -> (List Str)
  [
  "str-concat"
  "str-byte-length"
  "str-byte"
  "str-slice"
  "ref"
  "deref"
  "set!"
  "sb-new"
  "sb-append!"
  "sb-append-byte!"
  "sb-take-str!"
  "map-new"
  "map-set"
  "map-get"
  "map-has"
  "map-size"
  "mn-env-0"
  "mn-env-1"
  "mn-env-get"
  "mn-closure-new"
  "mn-apply-0"
  "mn-apply-1"
  "mn-apply-2"
  "arg-count"
  "arg"
  "read-file"
  "write-file"
  "show"
  "mn-env-new"
  "mn-env-set"
  "compare"
  "sb-length"
  "sb-to-str"
  "dump"
  "spawn"
  "spawn-capture"
  "getenv"
  "exists"
  "rename"
  "isatty"
  "mtime"
  "cwd"
  "ensure-dir"
  "list-dir"
  "realpath"
  "now-ms"
  "remove"
  "is-dir"
  "mn_isatty"
  "mn_mtime"
  "mn_cwd"
  "mn_ensure_dir"
  "mn_list_dir"
  "mn_realpath"
  "mn_now_ms"
  "mn_remove"
  "mn_is_dir"
  "mn_arg_count"
  "mn_arg"
  "mn_read_file"
  "mn_write_file"
  "mn_spawn"
  "mn_spawn_capture"
  "mn_getenv"
  "mn_exists"
  "mn_rename"
  "f+"
  "f-"
  "f*"
  "f/"])

; `extern` declares the C symbol (`mn_exists`). Ambient compiler calls
; still use the Menard name (`exists`). Both lower to the same abs id.
(defn seam-menard-name (hn: Str) -> Str
  (if (= hn "mn_arg_count") "arg-count"
    (if (= hn "mn_arg") "arg"
      (if (= hn "mn_read_file") "read-file"
        (if (= hn "mn_write_file") "write-file"
          (if (= hn "mn_spawn") "spawn"
            (if (= hn "mn_spawn_capture") "spawn-capture"
            (if (= hn "mn_getenv") "getenv"
              (if (= hn "mn_exists") "exists"
                (if (= hn "mn_rename") "rename" (os-menard-name hn)))))))))))

(defn os-menard-name (hn: Str) -> Str
  (if (= hn "mn_isatty") "isatty"
    (if (= hn "mn_mtime") "mtime"
      (if (= hn "mn_cwd") "cwd"
        (if (= hn "mn_ensure_dir") "ensure-dir"
          (if (= hn "mn_list_dir") "list-dir"
            (if (= hn "mn_realpath") "realpath"
              (if (= hn "mn_now_ms") "now-ms"
                (if (= hn "mn_remove") "remove"
                  (if (= hn "mn_is_dir") "is-dir" hn))))))))))

(defn effect-alias (hn: Str) -> Str
  (if (= hn "mn_write") "write"
    (if (= hn "mn_exit") "exit" hn)))

(defn runtime-op-abs (hn: Str) (ns: Int) -> Int
  (runtime-op-abs-named (seam-menard-name hn) ns))

(defn os-op-abs (hn: Str) (ns: Int) -> Int
  (if (= hn "isatty") (extern-isatty-abs ns)
    (if (= hn "mtime") (extern-mtime-abs ns)
      (if (= hn "cwd") (extern-cwd-abs ns)
        (if (= hn "ensure-dir") (extern-ensure-dir-abs ns)
          (if (= hn "list-dir") (extern-list-dir-abs ns)
            (if (= hn "realpath") (extern-realpath-abs ns)
              (if (= hn "now-ms") (extern-now-ms-abs ns)
                (if (= hn "remove") (extern-remove-abs ns)
                  (extern-is-dir-abs ns))))))))))

(defn runtime-op-abs-named (hn: Str) (ns: Int) -> Int
  (if (str-in-list hn ["isatty" "mtime" "cwd" "ensure-dir" "list-dir" "realpath" "now-ms" "remove" "is-dir"])
    (os-op-abs hn ns)
  (if (= hn "f+") (extern-fadd-abs ns)
    (if (= hn "f-") (extern-fsub-abs ns)
      (if (= hn "f*") (extern-fmul-abs ns)
        (if (= hn "f/") (extern-fdiv-abs ns)
  (if (= hn "str-concat") (extern-str-concat-abs ns)
    (if (= hn "str-byte-length") (extern-str-byte-length-abs ns)
      (if (= hn "str-byte") (extern-str-byte-abs ns)
        (if (= hn "str-slice") (extern-str-slice-abs ns)
          (if (= hn "ref") (extern-ref-new-abs ns)
            (if (= hn "deref") (extern-ref-deref-abs ns)
              (if (= hn "set!") (extern-ref-set-abs ns)
                (if (= hn "sb-new") (extern-sb-new-abs ns)
                  (if (= hn "sb-append!") (extern-sb-append-abs ns)
                    (if (= hn "sb-append-byte!") (extern-sb-append-byte-abs ns)
                      (if (= hn "sb-take-str!") (extern-sb-take-str-abs ns)
                        (if (= hn "map-new") (extern-map-new-abs ns)
                          (if (= hn "map-set") (extern-map-set-abs ns)
                            (if (= hn "map-get") (extern-map-get-abs ns)
                              (if (= hn "map-has") (extern-map-has-abs ns)
                                (if (= hn "map-size") (extern-map-size-abs ns)
                                  (if (= hn "mn-env-0") (extern-env-0-abs ns)
                                    (if (= hn "mn-env-1") (extern-env-1-abs ns)
                                      (if (= hn "mn-env-get") (extern-env-get-abs ns)
                                        (if (= hn "mn-closure-new") (extern-closure-new-abs ns)
                                          (if (= hn "mn-apply-0") (extern-apply-0-abs ns)
                                            (if (= hn "mn-apply-1") (extern-apply-1-abs ns)
                                              (if (= hn "mn-apply-2") (extern-apply-2-abs ns)
                                                (if (= hn "arg-count") (extern-arg-count-abs ns)
                                                  (if (= hn "arg") (extern-arg-abs ns)
                                                    (if (= hn "read-file") (extern-read-file-abs ns)
                                                      (if (= hn "write-file") (extern-write-file-abs ns)
                                                        (if (= hn "show") (extern-show-abs ns)
                                                          (if (= hn "mn-env-new") (extern-env-new-abs ns)
                                                            (if (= hn "mn-env-set") (extern-env-set-abs ns)
                                                              (if (= hn "compare") (extern-compare-abs ns)
                                                                (if (= hn "sb-length") (extern-sb-length-abs ns)
                                                                  (if (= hn "sb-to-str") (extern-sb-to-str-abs ns)
                                                                  (if (= hn "dump") (extern-dump-abs ns)
                                                                    (if (= hn "spawn") (extern-spawn-abs ns)
                                                                      (if (= hn "spawn-capture") (extern-spawn-capture-abs ns)
                                                                      (if (= hn "getenv") (extern-getenv-abs ns)
                                                                        (if (= hn "exists") (extern-exists-abs ns)
                                                              (extern-rename-abs ns)))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))

(defn runtime-op-arity (hn: Str) -> Int
  (runtime-op-arity-named (seam-menard-name hn)))

(defn runtime-op-arity-named (hn: Str) -> Int
  (if (or (= hn "cwd") (= hn "now-ms")) 0
  (if (str-in-list hn ["isatty" "mtime" "ensure-dir" "list-dir" "realpath" "remove" "is-dir"]) 1
  (if (or (= hn "sb-new") (= hn "map-new") (= hn "mn-env-0") (= hn "arg-count")) 0
    (if (str-in-list hn ["str-byte-length" "ref" "deref" "sb-take-str!" "map-size" "mn-env-1" "mn-env-new" "arg" "read-file" "mn-apply-0" "show" "sb-length" "sb-to-str" "dump" "spawn" "getenv" "exists"]) 1
      (if (or (= hn "str-slice") (= hn "map-set") (= hn "mn-apply-2") (= hn "mn-env-set")) 3
        2))))))

(defn lower-runtime-op (hn: Str) (args: (List Ast)) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (if (= hn "mn-closure-new")
    (lower-closure-new args env b funcs noop pool)
    (if (= (length args) (runtime-op-arity hn))
      (result-bind (lower-args args env b funcs noop pool)
        (fn (avs) (Ok (emit-call-words! b (runtime-op-abs hn (str-pool-count pool)) avs))))
      (Err (str-concat "arity mismatch calling " hn)))))

; `(mn-closure-new __lamN env)` — first arg is a FuncRef symbol; emit
; ptrtoint of that function's module-scope abs id, then call mn_closure_new.
(defn lower-closure-new (args: (List Ast)) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (match args
    [code-ast env-ast]
      (match (sym-str code-ast)
        (None) (Err "mn-closure-new requires a function name as its first argument")
        (Some lam-name)
          (match (map-get funcs lam-name)
            (None) (Err (str-concat "mn-closure-new: unknown function " lam-name))
            (Some fr)
              (do
                (let code-bits (emit-cast! b cast-ptrtoint (func-ref-abs fr) ty-i64))
                (result-bind (lower-expr env-ast env b funcs noop pool)
                  (fn (env-val) (Ok (emit-call! b (extern-closure-new-abs (str-pool-count pool)) [code-bits (get! b env-val)])))))))
    _ (Err "mn-closure-new requires a function name and an env")))

(defn is-wildcard-pat (pat: Ast) -> Bool
  (match pat (SymNode n _) (= n "_") _ false))

(defn pat-ctor-name (pat: Ast) -> (Maybe Str)
  (match pat
    (ParenNode (Cons head _) _) (sym-str head)
    (SymNode n _) (Some n)
    _ (None)))

(defn pat-payload-asts (pat: Ast) -> (List Ast)
  (match pat
    (ParenNode (Cons _ rest) _) rest
    _ []))

(defn is-upper-name (s: Str) -> Bool
  (let b (str-byte s 0))
  (and (>= b 65) (<= b 90)))

(defn bind-name! (name: Str) (val: Int) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) -> (Map Str Int)
  (do
    (let slot (root-alloca! b))
    (emit-store! b slot val)
    (map-set env name slot)))

; Bind `pat` against `val`. Constructor and literal mismatches branch to
; `else-bb` (not yet closed). Names, including nested payload names, are
; added to the returned env. `_` and uppercase nullary ctors bind nothing.
(defn bind-pat! (pat: Ast) (val: Int) (else-bb: BB) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result (Map Str Int) Str)
  (match pat
    (SymNode n _)
      (if (= n "_") (Ok env)
        (if (is-upper-name n) (bind-nullary-pat! n val else-bb env b pool)
          (Ok (bind-name! n val env b))))
    (ParenNode (Cons head args) _)
      (match (sym-str head)
        (Some cname) (bind-ctor-pat! cname args val else-bb env b pool)
        (None) (Err "unsupported match pattern"))
    (IntNode n _) (bind-int-pat! n val else-bb env b)
    (BoolNode flag _) (bind-bool-pat! flag val else-bb env b)
    (StrNode s _) (bind-str-pat! s val else-bb env b pool)
    _ (Err "unsupported match pattern")))

(defn bind-nullary-pat! (cname: Str) (val: Int) (else-bb: BB) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result (Map Str Int) Str)
  (bind-ctor-pat! cname [] val else-bb env b pool))

(defn bind-ctor-pat! (cname: Str) (payloads: (List Ast)) (val: Int) (else-bb: BB) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result (Map Str Int) Str)
  (match (ctor-tag-of cname pool)
    (None) (Err (str-concat "cannot lower match on constructor " cname))
    (Some want-tag)
      (do
        (let tag-abs (emit-call! b (extern-tag-abs (str-pool-count pool)) [val]))
        (let want (const-i64! b want-tag))
        (let cond (emit-cmp2! b icmp-eq tag-abs want))
        (let ok-bb (fresh-bb! b))
        (emit-condbr! b ok-bb else-bb cond)
        (switch-to! b ok-bb)
        (bind-payloads! payloads val 0 else-bb env b pool))))

(defn bind-payloads! (payloads: (List Ast)) (val: Int) (i: Int) (else-bb: BB) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result (Map Str Int) Str)
  (match payloads
    [] (Ok env)
    (Cons p rest)
      (do
        (let idx (const-i64! b i))
        (let slotv (emit-call! b (extern-slot-abs (str-pool-count pool)) [val idx]))
        (result-bind (bind-pat! p slotv else-bb env b pool)
          (fn (env2) (bind-payloads! rest val (+ i 1) else-bb env2 b pool))))))

(defn bind-bool-pat! (flag: Bool) (val: Int) (else-bb: BB) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) -> (Result (Map Str Int) Str)
  (bind-int-pat! (if flag 1 0) val else-bb env b))

(defn bind-int-pat! (n: Int) (val: Int) (else-bb: BB) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) -> (Result (Map Str Int) Str)
  (do
    (let lit (const-tagged! b n))
    (let cond (emit-cmp2! b icmp-eq val lit))
    (let ok-bb (fresh-bb! b))
    (emit-condbr! b ok-bb else-bb cond)
    (switch-to! b ok-bb)
    (Ok env)))

; `val` is the scrutinee word. Root it before `mn_str_new`: that allocation
; can copy, and a word held only in a register would not be updated.
(defn bind-str-pat! (s: Str) (val: Int) (else-bb: BB) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result (Map Str Int) Str)
  (do
    (let rooted (keep! b val))
    (let lit (keep! b (emit-str-lit! b pool s)))
    (let eqw (emit-call! b (extern-equal-abs (str-pool-count pool)) [(get! b rooted) (get! b lit)]))
    (let f (const-false! b))
    (let cond (emit-cmp2! b icmp-ne eqw f))
    (let ok-bb (fresh-bb! b))
    (emit-condbr! b ok-bb else-bb cond)
    (switch-to! b ok-bb)
    (Ok env)))

(defn lower-match (rest: (List Ast)) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (match rest
    (Cons scrut clauses)
      (result-bind (lower-expr scrut env b funcs noop pool)
        (fn (sv) (lower-match-with-scrut sv clauses env b funcs noop pool)))
    [] (Err "match requires a scrutinee")))

(defn lower-match-with-scrut (sv: Int) (clauses: (List Ast)) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (do
    (let result-slot (emit-alloca! b))
    (let join-bb (fresh-bb! b))
    (lower-match-clauses sv clauses result-slot join-bb env b funcs noop pool)))

(defn lower-match-clauses (sv: Int) (clauses: (List Ast)) (result-slot: Int) (join-bb: BB) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (match clauses
    []
      (do
        (emit-store! b result-slot (keep! b (const-tagged! b 0)))
        (emit-br! b join-bb)
        (switch-to! b join-bb)
        (Ok (get! b (emit-load! b result-slot))))
    (Cons pat (Cons body rest-clauses))
      (if (is-wildcard-pat pat)
        (lower-match-wildcard-body body result-slot join-bb env b funcs noop pool)
        (lower-match-pat-clause sv pat body rest-clauses result-slot join-bb env b funcs noop pool))
    [_] (Err "match clause missing a body")))

(defn lower-match-wildcard-body (body: Ast) (result-slot: Int) (join-bb: BB) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (result-bind (lower-expr body env b funcs noop pool)
    (fn (v)
      (do
        (maybe-store-and-br! b result-slot v join-bb)
        (switch-to! b join-bb)
        (Ok (get! b (emit-load! b result-slot)))))))

(defn lower-match-pat-clause (sv: Int) (pat: Ast) (body: Ast) (rest-clauses: (List Ast)) (result-slot: Int) (join-bb: BB) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (do
    (let else-bb (fresh-bb! b))
    (let val (get! b sv))
    (result-bind (bind-pat! pat val else-bb env b pool)
      (fn (env2)
        (result-bind (lower-expr body env2 b funcs noop pool)
          (fn (v)
            (do
              (maybe-store-and-br! b result-slot v join-bb)
              (switch-to! b else-bb)
              (lower-match-clauses sv rest-clauses result-slot join-bb env b funcs noop pool))))))))

; `if`'s test: a direct comparison (produces `i1` directly) or any
; Bool-valued expression (`icmp ne` against the `false` immediate).
(defn lower-cond (ast: Ast) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (match ast
    (ParenNode [head a c] _) (lower-cond-maybe-cmp head a c ast env b funcs noop pool)
    _ (lower-cond-bool-value ast env b funcs noop pool)))

(defn lower-cond-maybe-cmp (head: Ast) (a-ast: Ast) (c-ast: Ast) (whole: Ast) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (match (sym-str head)
    (Some hn) (if (is-cmp-op hn) (lower-cond-op hn a-ast c-ast env b funcs noop pool) (lower-cond-bool-value whole env b funcs noop pool))
    (None) (lower-cond-bool-value whole env b funcs noop pool)))

(defn lower-cond-op (hn: Str) (a-ast: Ast) (c-ast: Ast) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (result-bind (lower-expr a-ast env b funcs noop pool)
    (fn (av) (result-bind (lower-expr c-ast env b funcs noop pool)
      (fn (cv) (Ok (lower-cond-cmp! hn av cv b pool)))))))

; `=` is value-directed (`mn_equal`). Ordering ops stay immediate icmp.
(defn lower-cond-cmp! (hn: Str) (av: Int) (cv: Int) (b: Builder) (pool: StrPool) -> Int
  (if (= hn "=")
    (do
      (let eqw (emit-call! b (extern-equal-abs (str-pool-count pool)) [(get! b av) (get! b cv)]))
      (let f (const-false! b))
      (emit-cmp2! b icmp-ne eqw f))
    (emit-cmp2! b (cmp-pred-for hn) (get! b av) (get! b cv))))

(defn lower-cond-bool-value (ast: Ast) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (result-bind (lower-expr ast env b funcs noop pool)
    (fn (bv)
      (do
        (let f (const-false! b))
        (Ok (emit-cmp2! b icmp-ne (get! b bv) f))))))

; Comparison as a Bool *value* (not only as `if`'s test).
(defn lower-cmp-value (args: (List Ast)) (op: Str) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (match args
    [a-ast c-ast]
      (result-bind (lower-expr a-ast env b funcs noop pool)
        (fn (av) (result-bind (lower-expr c-ast env b funcs noop pool)
          (fn (cv) (Ok (lower-cmp-word! op av cv b pool))))))
    _ (Err (str-concat "comparison `" op "` expects exactly 2 arguments"))))

(defn lower-cmp-word! (op: Str) (av: Int) (cv: Int) (b: Builder) (pool: StrPool) -> Int
  (if (= op "=")
    (emit-call! b (extern-equal-abs (str-pool-count pool)) [(get! b av) (get! b cv)])
    (bool-from-i1! b (emit-cmp2! b (cmp-pred-for op) (get! b av) (get! b cv)))))

(defn cmp-pred-for (op: Str) -> Int
  (if (= op "<") icmp-slt
    (if (= op ">") icmp-sgt
      (if (= op "<=") icmp-sle
        (if (= op ">=") icmp-sge
          icmp-eq)))))

; -- arithmetic --

(defn lower-arith (args: (List Ast)) (op: Str) (sp: Span) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (match args
    [a-ast c-ast]
      (result-bind (lower-expr a-ast env b funcs noop pool)
        (fn (av) (result-bind (lower-expr c-ast env b funcs noop pool) (fn (cv) (Ok (apply-arith! b pool sp op av cv))))))
    _ (Err (str-concat "operator " op " expects exactly 2 arguments"))))

(defn apply-arith! (b: Builder) (pool: StrPool) (sp: Span) (op: Str) (av: Int) (cv: Int) -> Int
  (let aw (get! b av))
  (let cw (get! b cv))
  (let panic-at (extern-panic-at-abs (str-pool-count pool)))
  (let file-gid (file-gid-of pool (span-origin sp)))
  (let line (span-line-clamped sp))
  (let msg-gid (str-pool-get pool (div-zero-msg)))
  (if (= op "+") (arith-add! b aw cw)
    (if (= op "-") (arith-sub! b aw cw)
      (if (= op "*") (arith-mul! b aw cw)
        (if (= op "/") (arith-div! b panic-at file-gid line msg-gid aw cw)
          (arith-rem! b panic-at file-gid line msg-gid aw cw))))))

; -- let (both the inline-body form `(let n e body…)` and the bare,
; sequence-threading form `(let n e)` — see `lower-sequence` for the
; latter). --

(defn lower-let-inline (rest: (List Ast)) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (match rest
    (Cons name-ast (Cons expr-ast body)) (lower-let-inline-named name-ast expr-ast body env b funcs noop pool)
    _ (Err "let requires a name and an expression")))

(defn lower-let-inline-named (name-ast: Ast) (expr-ast: Ast) (body: (List Ast)) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (match (sym-str name-ast)
    (None) (Err "let name must be a symbol")
    (Some name) (result-bind (lower-expr expr-ast env b funcs noop pool) (fn (v) (lower-let-inline-bind name v body env b funcs noop pool)))))

(defn lower-let-inline-bind (name: Str) (v: Int) (body: (List Ast)) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (do
    (let w (get! b v))
    (let slot (root-alloca! b))
    (emit-store! b slot w)
    (lower-let-inline-continue body (map-set env name slot) b funcs noop pool w)))

(defn lower-let-inline-continue (body: (List Ast)) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) (v: Int) -> (Result Int Str)
  (match body
    [] (Ok v)
    _ (lower-sequence body env b funcs noop pool)))

; -- sequences: a `defn` body (or a `do`'s tail) is a `(List Ast)` of
; sequential forms; a bare `(let n e)` among them extends the env for
; every sibling that follows; a call to a known no-op (`shadow-push`/
; `shadow-pop`) is skipped entirely (see header comment). --

(defrec SimpleLet (name: Str) (expr: Ast))

(defn as-simple-let (f: Ast) -> (Maybe SimpleLet)
  (match f
    (ParenNode [head name-ast expr-ast] _) (as-simple-let-named head name-ast expr-ast)
    _ (None)))

(defn as-simple-let-named (head: Ast) (name-ast: Ast) (expr-ast: Ast) -> (Maybe SimpleLet)
  (if (is-sym head "let")
    (match (sym-str name-ast) (Some n) (Some (SimpleLet n expr-ast)) (None) (None))
    (None)))

(defn is-unit-noop-call (f: Ast) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) -> Bool
  (match f
    (ParenNode [head] _) (is-unit-noop-call-named head noop)
    _ false))

(defn is-unit-noop-call-named (head: Ast) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) -> Bool
  (match (sym-str head)
    (None) false
    (Some name) (match (map-get noop name) (Some _) true (None) false)))

; -- `println`/`print`/`write`: Unit-producing "effect" steps, usable
; only mid-sequence (never a body's last form — see header comment's
; "Unit results") — see `StrPool`'s doc comment (below `lower-program`)
; for the two-pass string-global scheme these lower against.

(defn is-effect-head (s: Str) -> Bool
  (or (= s "println")
      (= s "print")
      (= s "write")
      (= s "exit")
      (= s "mn_write")
      (= s "mn_exit")))

(defn is-effect-call (f: Ast) -> Bool
  (match f
    (ParenNode (Cons head _) _) (is-effect-call-named head)
    _ false))

(defn is-effect-call-named (head: Ast) -> Bool
  (match (sym-str head)
    (Some n) (is-effect-head n)
    (None) false))

; A one-byte "\n" `Str`, `println`'s own trailing newline — built the
; same way `src/mn.mnd`'s `nl` is, and deliberately run through the
; very same `StrPool` (deduped by content) every `println` call needs,
; rather than kept as some separate always-present global: a program
; with no `println` at all pays for zero string globals, not one.
(defn newline-str -> Str
  (do
    (let sb (sb-new))
    (sb-append-byte! sb 10)
    (sb-take-str! sb)))

; Trailing 0 so `mn_panic`'s `strlen` stops at the end of the message.
; The pool stores the bytes as given; a Menard string literal has no NUL.
(defn div-zero-msg -> Str
  (do
    (let sb (sb-new))
    (sb-append! sb "division by zero")
    (sb-append-byte! sb 0)
    (sb-take-str! sb)))

(defn lower-effect (f: Ast) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Unit Str)
  (match f
    (ParenNode (Cons head rest) _) (lower-effect-named head rest env b funcs noop pool)
    _ (Err "not an effect call")))

(defn lower-effect-named (head: Ast) (rest: (List Ast)) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Unit Str)
  (match (sym-str head)
    (None) (Err "not an effect call")
    (Some hn) (lower-effect-op hn rest env b funcs noop pool)))

(defn lower-effect-op (hn: Str) (rest: (List Ast)) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Unit Str)
  (lower-effect-known (effect-alias hn) rest env b funcs noop pool))

(defn lower-effect-known (hn: Str) (rest: (List Ast)) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Unit Str)
  (if (= hn "println") (lower-println rest env b funcs noop pool)
    (if (= hn "print") (lower-print rest env b funcs noop pool)
      (if (= hn "exit") (lower-exit rest env b funcs noop pool)
        (lower-write rest env b funcs noop pool)))))

; `(exit code)` — noreturn via `mn_exit` (tagged Int in, untagged inside).
(defn lower-exit (rest: (List Ast)) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Unit Str)
  (match rest
    [code-ast]
      (result-bind (lower-expr code-ast env b funcs noop pool)
        (fn (v) (Ok (emit-call-void! b extern-kind-print (extern-exit-abs (str-pool-count pool)) [(get! b v)]))))
    _ (Err "exit requires exactly one Int argument")))

; `println`/`print`'s variadic args: each is either a `Str` literal
; (written directly to fd 1, byte for byte) or an `Int`-valued
; expression (untagged and written via `mn_print_i64`) — anything else
; (a `Bool`, a non-literal `Str`, …) is a clean `Err`, same rationale as
; every other not-yet-supported value shape in this module.
(defn lower-print-args (args: (List Ast)) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Unit Str)
  (match args
    [] (Ok ())
    (Cons a rest) (result-then (lower-print-arg a env b funcs noop pool) (fn () (lower-print-args rest env b funcs noop pool)))))

(defn lower-print-arg (a: Ast) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Unit Str)
  (match a
    (StrNode s _) (Ok (emit-write-str-to! b pool s (str-pool-write-stdout-abs pool)))
    _ (lower-print-int-arg a env b funcs noop pool)))

(defn lower-print-int-arg (a: Ast) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Unit Str)
  (result-bind (lower-expr a env b funcs noop pool) (fn (v) (Ok (emit-print-i64! b pool v)))))

(defn lower-print (args: (List Ast)) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Unit Str)
  (lower-print-args args env b funcs noop pool))

(defn lower-println (args: (List Ast)) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Unit Str)
  (result-then (lower-print-args args env b funcs noop pool) (fn () (Ok (emit-write-str-to! b pool (newline-str) (str-pool-write-stdout-abs pool))))))

; `(write fd s)` — literal fd 1/2 with a literal or (for fd 1) any Str keeps
; the direct stdout/stderr externs. A computed fd, or a computed Str on
; fd 2, goes through `mn_write`.
(defn lower-write-any (fd-ast: Ast) (s-ast: Ast) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Unit Str)
  (result-bind (lower-expr fd-ast env b funcs noop pool)
    (fn (fd)
      (result-bind (lower-expr s-ast env b funcs noop pool)
        (fn (s)
          (Ok (do
            (emit-call! b (extern-write-abs (str-pool-count pool)) [(get! b fd) (get! b s)])
            ())))))))

(defn lower-write-str (s-ast: Ast) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) (callee-abs: Int) (is-stdout: Bool) -> (Result Unit Str)
  (match s-ast
    (StrNode s _) (Ok (emit-write-str-to! b pool s callee-abs))
    _ (if is-stdout
        (result-bind (lower-expr s-ast env b funcs noop pool)
          (fn (v) (Ok (emit-call-void! b extern-kind-print (extern-print-str-abs (str-pool-count pool)) [(get! b v)]))))
        (lower-write-any (IntNode 2 (Span 0 0 0 1)) s-ast env b funcs noop pool))))

(defn lower-write (rest: (List Ast)) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Unit Str)
  (match rest
    [fd-ast s-ast] (lower-write-fd fd-ast s-ast env b funcs noop pool)
    _ (Err "write requires exactly two arguments: a file descriptor and a Str")))

(defn lower-write-fd (fd-ast: Ast) (s-ast: Ast) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Unit Str)
  (match fd-ast
    (IntNode n _) (lower-write-fd-n n s-ast env b funcs noop pool)
    _ (lower-write-any fd-ast s-ast env b funcs noop pool)))

(defn lower-write-fd-n (n: Int) (s-ast: Ast) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Unit Str)
  (if (= n 1)
    (lower-write-str s-ast env b funcs noop pool (str-pool-write-stdout-abs pool) true)
    (if (= n 2)
      (lower-write-str s-ast env b funcs noop pool (str-pool-write-stderr-abs pool) false)
      (Err "write's file descriptor must be the Int literal 1 or 2"))))

(defn lower-sequence (forms: (List Ast)) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (match forms
    [] (Err "an empty body cannot be lowered to an Int")
    (Cons f rest) (lower-sequence-step f rest env b funcs noop pool)))

(defn lower-sequence-step (f: Ast) (rest: (List Ast)) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (if (is-unit-noop-call f noop)
    (lower-sequence-after-skip rest env b funcs noop pool)
    (if (is-effect-call f)
      (lower-sequence-effect f rest env b funcs noop pool)
      (lower-sequence-step-real f rest env b funcs noop pool))))

(defn lower-sequence-after-skip (rest: (List Ast)) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (match rest
    [] (Err "a no-op call cannot be the last form of a body")
    _ (lower-sequence rest env b funcs noop pool)))

; `println`/`print`/`write` produce `Unit`, never an `Int` — exactly the
; same "cannot be the body's last form" restriction a no-op skip already
; has (see header comment's "Unit results"); lowering the effect itself
; (real `mn_write_stdout`/`mn_print_i64` calls) happens here, then
; `rest` continues exactly like a skipped no-op would.
(defn lower-sequence-effect (f: Ast) (rest: (List Ast)) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (result-then (lower-effect f env b funcs noop pool) (fn () (lower-sequence-after-effect rest env b funcs noop pool))))

(defn lower-sequence-after-effect (rest: (List Ast)) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (match rest
    [] (Ok (const-unit! b))
    _ (lower-sequence rest env b funcs noop pool)))

(defn lower-sequence-step-real (f: Ast) (rest: (List Ast)) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (match (as-simple-let f)
    (Some sl) (lower-sequence-let sl rest env b funcs noop pool)
    (None) (lower-sequence-plain f rest env b funcs noop pool)))

(defn lower-sequence-let (sl: SimpleLet) (rest: (List Ast)) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (match sl
    (SimpleLet name expr) (result-bind (lower-expr expr env b funcs noop pool) (fn (v) (lower-sequence-let-bind name v rest env b funcs noop pool)))))

(defn lower-sequence-let-bind (name: Str) (v: Int) (rest: (List Ast)) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (do
    (let w (get! b v))
    (let slot (root-alloca! b))
    (emit-store! b slot w)
    (lower-sequence-rest rest (map-set env name slot) b funcs noop pool w)))

(defn lower-sequence-rest (rest: (List Ast)) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) (fallback: Int) -> (Result Int Str)
  (match rest
    [] (Ok fallback)
    _ (lower-sequence rest env b funcs noop pool)))

(defn lower-sequence-plain (f: Ast) (rest: (List Ast)) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (result-bind (lower-expr f env b funcs noop pool) (fn (v) (lower-sequence-rest rest env b funcs noop pool (get! b v)))))

; -- calls to other top-level `Int`-only `defn`s --

(defn lower-args (arg-asts: (List Ast)) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result (List Int) Str)
  (match arg-asts
    [] (Ok [])
    (Cons a rest) (result-bind (lower-expr a env b funcs noop pool) (fn (v) (lower-args-cons v rest env b funcs noop pool)))))

(defn lower-args-cons (v: Int) (rest: (List Ast)) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result (List Int) Str)
  (result-bind (lower-args rest env b funcs noop pool) (fn (vs) (Ok (Cons v vs)))))

(defn lower-call (name: Str) (arg-asts: (List Ast)) (sp: Span) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (match (map-get funcs name)
    (Some fr) (lower-call-with-ref fr name arg-asts sp env b funcs noop pool)
    (None) (lower-call-local-or-err name arg-asts sp env b funcs noop pool)))

; A local holding a heap closure: `(f arg)` → `mn_apply_1`.
(defn lower-call-local-or-err (name: Str) (arg-asts: (List Ast)) (sp: Span) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (match (map-get env name)
    (None) (Err (str-concat "cannot lower a call to " name))
    (Some slot) (lower-apply-local slot name arg-asts sp env b funcs noop pool)))

(defn lower-apply-local (slot: Int) (name: Str) (arg-asts: (List Ast)) (sp: Span) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (match arg-asts
    []
      (do
        (let clo (emit-load! b slot))
        (Ok (emit-traced-call! b pool sp (extern-apply-0-abs (str-pool-count pool)) [clo])))
    [a0]
      (result-bind (lower-expr a0 env b funcs noop pool)
        (fn (arg)
          (do
            (let clo (emit-load! b slot))
            (Ok (emit-traced-call! b pool sp (extern-apply-1-abs (str-pool-count pool)) [clo (get! b arg)])))))
    [a0 a1]
      (result-bind (lower-expr a0 env b funcs noop pool)
        (fn (arg0)
          (result-bind (lower-expr a1 env b funcs noop pool)
            (fn (arg1)
              (do
                (let clo (emit-load! b slot))
                (Ok (emit-traced-call! b pool sp (extern-apply-2-abs (str-pool-count pool))
                  [clo (get! b arg0) (get! b arg1)])))))))
    _ (Err (str-concat "closure application supports 0–2 arguments (calling local `" name "`)"))))

(defn lower-call-with-ref (fr: FuncRef) (name: Str) (arg-asts: (List Ast)) (sp: Span) (env: (Map Str Int)) (b: Builder) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) -> (Result Int Str)
  (if (= (length arg-asts) (func-ref-arity fr))
    (result-bind (lower-args arg-asts env b funcs noop pool) (fn (args) (Ok (emit-traced-call! b pool sp (func-ref-abs fr) (get-words! b args)))))
    (Err (str-concat "arity mismatch calling " name))))

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; One function: bind params (each its own alloca, uniformly with `let`s
; — see header comment), lower the body, then either `ret` the tagged
; `i64` result directly, or — `main` only — untag+trunc to `i32` first.

(defn bind-params! (b: Builder) (names: (List Str)) (start: Int) (i: Int) -> (Map Str Int)
  (match names
    [] (map-new)
    (Cons n rest) (bind-params-cons! b n rest start i)))

(defn bind-params-cons! (b: Builder) (n: Str) (rest: (List Str)) (start: Int) (i: Int) -> (Map Str Int)
  (do
    (let param-abs (+ start i))
    (let slot (root-alloca! b))
    (emit-store! b slot param-abs)
    (map-set (bind-params! b rest start (+ i 1)) n slot)))

(defn finish-return! (b: Builder) (is-main: Bool) (result-abs: Int) -> Unit
  (do
    (emit-root-restore! b (deref (b-root-base b)))
    (if is-main (finish-main-return! b result-abs) (emit-ret! b result-abs))))

; spec: `main` computes a tagged `i64` `Int` like any other function,
; then `lshr 1` (untag) + `trunc i32` + `ret i32` — see header comment.
(defn finish-main-return! (b: Builder) (result-abs: Int) -> Unit
  (do
    (let one (const-i64! b 1))
    (let untagged (emit-binop! b binop-lshr result-abs one))
    (let i32v (emit-cast! b cast-trunc untagged ty-i32))
    (emit-ret! b i32v)))

(defn lower-one-func (ld: LDefn) (num-globals: Int) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) (mc: (Map Str Bool)) -> (Result LFunc Str)
  (do
    (let is-main (= (ldefn-name ld) "main"))
    ; Native `@main` is `(i32 argc, ptr argv) -> i32` — two LLVM params that
    ; are not Menard words; Menard `main` itself still takes zero args.
    (let llvm-nparams (if is-main 2 (param-arity-of (ldefn-params ld))))
    (let b (builder-new (+ num-globals llvm-nparams)))
    (let flag (match (map-get mc (ldefn-name ld)) (Some f) f (None) true))
    (set! (b-rooting b) flag)
    (set! (b-root-ns b) (str-pool-count pool))
    (if flag (set! (b-root-base b) (emit-root-save! b)) ())
    (let env0 (bind-params! b (lparam-names (ldefn-params ld)) num-globals 0))
    (emit-main-init-if-needed! b is-main num-globals pool)
    (match (lower-sequence (ldefn-body ld) env0 b funcs noop pool)
      (Ok result-abs) (lower-one-func-finish ld is-main result-abs b)
      (Err msg) (Err (str-concat (ldefn-name ld) ": " msg)))))

; Call `mn_init(argc, argv)` at the start of `main` so `arg` / `arg-count`
; see the process argv. Param abs ids are `num-globals` and `num-globals+1`.
(defn emit-main-init-if-needed! (b: Builder) (is-main: Bool) (num-globals: Int) (pool: StrPool) -> Unit
  (if is-main
    (emit-call-void! b extern-kind-init (extern-init-abs (str-pool-count pool))
      [num-globals (+ num-globals 1)])
    ()))

; libc already defines `write`, `stdin`, `stdout`, and `stderr`. Menard
; functions keep their source names for calls; the link symbol is prefixed
; so a published `(defn write ...)` does not replace the syscall.
; `main` is the bootstrap C entry. `mn_<hash>_…` is already the link symbol
; of a module `main` or init (see `modules/graph.mnd`).
(defn is-mn-symbol (name: Str) -> Bool
  (and (>= (str-byte-length name) 3) (= (str-slice name 0 3) "mn_")))

(defn link-symbol (name: Str) -> Str
  (if (or (= name "main") (is-mn-symbol name)) name (str-concat "menard." name)))

(defn lower-one-func-finish (ld: LDefn) (is-main: Bool) (result-abs: Int) (b: Builder) -> (Result LFunc Str)
  (do
    (finish-return! b is-main result-abs)
    (finish-builder! b)
    (Ok (LFunc (link-symbol (ldefn-name ld)) (param-arity-of (ldefn-params ld)) is-main (total-blocks b) (builder-items-ordered b)))))

(defn lower-all-funcs (lds: (List LDefn)) (num-globals: Int) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) (mc: (Map Str Bool)) -> (Result (List LFunc) Str)
  (match lds
    [] (Ok [])
    (Cons ld rest) (result-bind (lower-one-func ld num-globals funcs noop pool mc)
      (fn (lf) (lower-all-funcs-cons lf rest num-globals funcs noop pool mc)))))

(defn lower-all-funcs-cons (lf: LFunc) (rest: (List LDefn)) (num-globals: Int) (funcs: (Map Str FuncRef)) (noop: (Map Str Bool)) (pool: StrPool) (mc: (Map Str Bool)) -> (Result (List LFunc) Str)
  (result-bind (lower-all-funcs rest num-globals funcs noop pool mc) (fn (lfs) (Ok (Cons lf lfs)))))

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Top-level, non-`defn` forms — `hello.mnd`'s standalone `(println
; "Hello, world!")` and `123`, run for effect before `main`'s own body
; (see header comment's "Lowering", point 1). Only *bare expression*
; forms are collected this way — a top-level `defrec`/`variant`/`alias`
; (or a `pub`-wrapped one) is a type declaration, not something with a
; value to compute, and is left exactly as un-lowered as it always was
; (this module has never lowered those, and does not start now); only
; skipping them here, rather than trying to lower them as if they were
; expressions, keeps that behavior unchanged for any program that has
; one.
(defn is-declaration-head (s: Str) -> Bool
  (or (= s "defn")
      (= s "defrec")
      (= s "variant")
      (= s "alias")
      (= s "extern")
      (= s "import")))

(defn is-declaration-form (ast: Ast) -> Bool
  (match (unwrap-pub ast)
    (ParenNode (Cons head _) _) (is-declaration-form-named head)
    _ false))

(defn is-declaration-form-named (head: Ast) -> Bool
  (match (sym-str head)
    (Some n) (is-declaration-head n)
    (None) false))

(defn collect-non-defn-tops (forms: (List Ast)) -> (List Ast)
  (match forms
    [] []
    (Cons f rest) (collect-non-defn-tops-cons f rest)))

(defn collect-non-defn-tops-cons (f: Ast) (rest: (List Ast)) -> (List Ast)
  (if (is-declaration-form f) (collect-non-defn-tops rest) (Cons f (collect-non-defn-tops rest))))

(defn append-asts (xs: (List Ast)) (ys: (List Ast)) -> (List Ast)
  (match xs [] ys (Cons x rest) (Cons x (append-asts rest ys))))

; Splices `extra` onto the *front* of `main`'s own body — `main`'s last
; form (its real `Int` result) stays last; `extra`'s forms (run purely
; for effect, per `collect-non-defn-tops`) run first, in source order.
; Every other `LDefn` in `lds` passes through unchanged.
(defn replace-main-body (lds: (List LDefn)) (extra: (List Ast)) -> (List LDefn)
  (match lds
    [] []
    (Cons ld rest) (replace-main-body-cons ld rest extra)))

(defn replace-main-body-cons (ld: LDefn) (rest: (List LDefn)) (extra: (List Ast)) -> (List LDefn)
  (if (= (ldefn-name ld) "main")
    (Cons (LDefn (ldefn-name ld) (ldefn-params ld) (ldefn-ret ld) (append-asts extra (ldefn-body ld))) rest)
    (Cons ld (replace-main-body rest extra))))

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Entry point: find `main`, lower every `Int`-only top-level `defn` (in
; source order — this order is the module's global value numbering, see
; header comment), hand the result to `bc-writer.mnd`.

; A top-level `(let stdout 1)` is a value, not a function. Uses of the name
; become the integer, so `(write stdout s)` lowers like `(write 1 s)`.
(defn add-int-constant (ast: Ast) (acc: (Map Str Int)) -> (Map Str Int)
  (match (unwrap-pub ast)
    (ParenNode [head name-ast expr] _)
      (if (is-sym head "let")
        (add-int-constant-named name-ast expr acc)
        acc)
    _ acc))

(defn add-int-constant-named (name-ast: Ast) (expr: Ast) (acc: (Map Str Int)) -> (Map Str Int)
  (match (sym-str name-ast)
    (None) acc
    (Some n)
      (match expr
        (IntNode k _) (map-set acc n k)
        _ acc)))

(defn collect-int-constants-from (forms: (List Ast)) (acc: (Map Str Int)) -> (Map Str Int)
  (match forms
    [] acc
    (Cons f rest) (collect-int-constants-from rest (add-int-constant f acc))))

(defn collect-int-constants (forms: (List Ast)) -> (Map Str Int)
  (collect-int-constants-from forms (map-new)))

(defn name-is-bound (name: Str) (bound: (List Str)) -> Bool
  (match bound
    [] false
    (Cons b rest) (if (= name b) true (name-is-bound name rest))))

(defn subst-list (xs: (List Ast)) (consts: (Map Str Int)) (bound: (List Str)) -> (List Ast)
  (match xs
    [] []
    (Cons x rest) (Cons (subst-const x consts bound) (subst-list rest consts bound))))

(defn subst-sym (name: Str) (sp: Span) (consts: (Map Str Int)) (bound: (List Str)) -> Ast
  (if (name-is-bound name bound) (SymNode name sp)
    (match (map-get consts name)
      (Some k) (IntNode k sp)
      (None) (SymNode name sp))))

(defn let-bound-name (name-ast: Ast) -> Str
  (match (sym-str name-ast) (Some n) n (None) ""))

; A parameter is `(name: Type)` or a bare symbol. The colon is part of the
; symbol text. The name shadows an integer constant of the same spelling,
; so `(stdin: Str)` is not `(let stdin 0)`.
(defn strip-trailing-colon (raw: Str) -> Str
  (let n (str-byte-length raw))
  (if (and (> n 0) (= (str-byte raw (- n 1)) 58)) (str-slice raw 0 (- n 1)) raw))

(defn param-bound-name (a: Ast) -> Str
  (match a
    (ParenNode (Cons n _) _) (strip-trailing-colon (let-bound-name n))
    (SymNode n _) (strip-trailing-colon n)
    _ ""))

(defn subst-let (elems: (List Ast)) (sp: Span) (consts: (Map Str Int)) (bound: (List Str)) -> Ast
  (match elems
    (Cons head (Cons name rest))
      (ParenNode (Cons head (Cons name (subst-list rest consts (Cons (let-bound-name name) bound)))) sp)
    _ (ParenNode (subst-list elems consts bound) sp)))

; Binders before `->` stay as written. The return type stays as written.
; Only the body is substituted, with the parameter names bound.
(defn subst-defn-body (xs: (List Ast)) (consts: (Map Str Int)) (bound: (List Str)) -> (List Ast)
  (match xs
    [] []
    (Cons ret body) (Cons ret (subst-list body consts bound))))

(defn subst-defn-params (xs: (List Ast)) (consts: (Map Str Int)) (bound: (List Str)) -> (List Ast)
  (match xs
    [] []
    (Cons x rest)
      (if (is-sym x "->")
        (Cons x (subst-defn-body rest consts bound))
        (Cons x (subst-defn-params rest consts (Cons (param-bound-name x) bound))))))

(defn subst-defn (elems: (List Ast)) (sp: Span) (consts: (Map Str Int)) (bound: (List Str)) -> Ast
  (match elems
    (Cons head (Cons name rest))
      (ParenNode (Cons head (Cons name (subst-defn-params rest consts bound))) sp)
    _ (ParenNode (subst-list elems consts bound) sp)))

(defn subst-paren (elems: (List Ast)) (sp: Span) (consts: (Map Str Int)) (bound: (List Str)) -> Ast
  (match elems
    (Cons head _)
      (if (is-sym head "quote") (ParenNode elems sp)
        (if (is-sym head "let") (subst-let elems sp consts bound)
          (if (or (is-sym head "defn") (is-sym head "fn"))
            (subst-defn elems sp consts bound)
            (ParenNode (subst-list elems consts bound) sp))))
    _ (ParenNode elems sp)))

(defn subst-const (ast: Ast) (consts: (Map Str Int)) (bound: (List Str)) -> Ast
  (match ast
    (SymNode name sp) (subst-sym name sp consts bound)
    (ParenNode elems sp) (subst-paren elems sp consts bound)
    (BracketNode elems sp) (BracketNode (subst-list elems consts bound) sp)
    _ ast))

(defn subst-forms (forms: (List Ast)) (consts: (Map Str Int)) -> (List Ast)
  (match forms
    [] []
    (Cons f rest) (Cons (subst-const f consts []) (subst-forms rest consts))))

(defn subst-int-constants (forms: (List Ast)) -> (List Ast)
  (subst-forms forms (collect-int-constants forms)))

; A top-level `(let end-block-code 0)` has already been substituted at every
; use. Leaving the binding in `main` would only store a dead integer.
(defn is-folded-int-let (ast: Ast) -> Bool
  (match (unwrap-pub ast)
    (ParenNode [head _ expr] _)
      (if (is-sym head "let")
        (match expr (IntNode _ _) true _ false)
        false)
    _ false))

(defn drop-folded-int-lets (forms: (List Ast)) -> (List Ast)
  (match forms
    [] []
    (Cons f rest)
      (if (is-folded-int-let f) (drop-folded-int-lets rest)
        (Cons f (drop-folded-int-lets rest)))))

(pub defn lower-program (forms: (List Ast)) (triple: Str) (paths: (List Str)) -> (Result Str Str)
  (lower-program-collected (drop-folded-int-lets (subst-int-constants forms)) triple paths))

(defn lower-program-collected (forms: (List Ast)) (triple: Str) (paths: (List Str)) -> (Result Str Str)
  (do
    (let lds (collect-ldefns-all forms))
    (let word-lds (filter-word-ldefns lds))
    (match (find-ldefn-named word-lds "main")
      (None) (Err "program has no top-level `defn main -> Int …` the real instruction lowerer can handle (`main` must return Int; helpers may use Int/Bool/Unit words)")
      (Some main-ld) (lower-program-checked-main main-ld word-lds lds forms triple paths))))

(defn lower-program-checked-main (main-ld: LDefn) (word-lds: (List LDefn)) (all-lds: (List LDefn)) (forms: (List Ast)) (triple: Str) (paths: (List Str)) -> (Result Str Str)
  (if (> (param-arity-of (ldefn-params main-ld)) 0)
    (Err "`main` must take no arguments")
    (if (or (is-int-type (ldefn-ret main-ld)) (is-unit-type (ldefn-ret main-ld)))
      (lower-program-build word-lds all-lds forms triple paths [] [])
      (Err "`main` must return Int or Unit"))))

; Global value numbering (see `llvm-ir.mnd`'s header comment and this
; module's `StrPool` doc comment): string globals first (`0..num-
; strings-1`), then the four fixed runtime externs, then every
; word-`defn` in source order — `build-func-refs`'s starting `idx`
; moves from `0` to `num-strings + extern-count` accordingly. Every
; function's own *local* value numbering must start after *all* of that,
; plus the module-level string-initializer constants `write-module-bc`
; also interleaves right after every declaration (one per string, same
; count again) — `num-globals` below is `2*num-strings + extern-count +
; num-funcs`, exactly what `write-module-body!`'s own `init-base` (`bc-
; writer.mnd`) assumes too.
; A function may-collect when it, or something it calls, can reach
; `mn_alloc`. Allocation-free functions are not rooted (spec §4.4).
; Unknown calls are treated as may-collect: over-rooting is safe.
(defn mc-pure (hn: Str) -> Bool
  (mc-pure-body (effect-alias (seam-menard-name hn))))

(defn mc-pure-body (hn: Str) -> Bool
  (or (str-in-list hn ["isatty" "mtime" "now-ms" "ensure-dir" "remove" "is-dir"])
      (= hn "if")
      (= hn "let")
      (= hn "do")
      (= hn "loop")
      (= hn "recur")
      (= hn "match")
      (= hn "println")
      (= hn "print")
      (= hn "shadow-push")
      (= hn "shadow-pop")
      (= hn "write")
      (= hn "exit")
      (= hn "deref")
      (= hn "set!")
      (= hn "str-byte")
      (= hn "str-byte-length")
      (= hn "map-has")
      (= hn "map-size")
      (= hn "mn-env-get")
      (= hn "arg-count")
      (= hn "exists")
      (= hn "sb-length")
      (= hn "sb-to-str")
      (= hn "dump")
      (= hn "+")
      (= hn "-")
      (= hn "*")
      (= hn "/")
      (= hn "%")
      (= hn "<")
      (= hn ">")
      (= hn "<=")
      (= hn ">=")
      (= hn "=")
      (= hn "compare")))

(defn mc-alloc-name (hn: Str) -> Bool
  (mc-alloc-body (seam-menard-name hn)))

(defn mc-alloc-body (hn: Str) -> Bool
  (or (= hn "str-concat")
      (= hn "str-slice")
      (= hn "ref")
      (= hn "sb-new")
      (= hn "sb-append!")
      (= hn "sb-append-byte!")
      (= hn "sb-take-str!")
      (= hn "map-new")
      (= hn "map-set")
      (= hn "map-get")
      (= hn "mn-env-0")
      (= hn "mn-env-1")
      (= hn "mn-env-new")
      (= hn "mn-closure-new")
      (= hn "mn-apply-0")
      (= hn "mn-apply-1")
      (= hn "mn-apply-2")
      (= hn "arg")
      (= hn "read-file")
      (= hn "write-file")
      (= hn "show")
      (= hn "spawn")
      (= hn "spawn-capture")
      (= hn "getenv")
      (= hn "rename")
      (= hn "f+")
      (= hn "f-")
      (= hn "f*")
      (= hn "f/")
      (= hn "cwd")
      (= hn "list-dir")
      (= hn "realpath")))

(defn mc-ctor-alloc (hn: Str) -> Bool
  (and (is-upper-name hn) (not (= hn "Nil")) (not (= hn "None"))))

; One walk records direct allocs and the user-function callees. Later
; passes only follow that graph, so the AST is not re-walked per pass.
(defrec McWalk (direct: Bool) (callees: (List Str)))

(defn mc-walk-empty -> McWalk (McWalk false []))

(defn mc-append (xs: (List Str)) (ys: (List Str)) -> (List Str)
  (match xs [] ys (Cons x rest) (Cons x (mc-append rest ys))))

(defn mc-walk-or (a: McWalk) (b: McWalk) -> McWalk
  (match a
    (McWalk da ca)
      (match b
        (McWalk db cb) (McWalk (or da db) (mc-append ca cb)))))

(defn mc-note-head (hn: Str) (names: (Map Str Bool)) -> McWalk
  (if (mc-pure hn) (mc-walk-empty)
    (if (or (mc-alloc-name hn) (mc-ctor-alloc hn)) (McWalk true [])
      (match (map-get names hn)
        (Some _) (McWalk false [hn])
        (None) (McWalk true [])))))

(defn mc-walk-forms (xs: (List Ast)) (names: (Map Str Bool)) -> McWalk
  (match xs
    [] (mc-walk-empty)
    (Cons a rest) (mc-walk-or (mc-walk-ast a names) (mc-walk-forms rest names))))

; A string literal lowers to `mn_str_new`. That allocation is not a call
; in the AST, so it has to count on its own — otherwise a function whose
; only allocation is `"..." ` keeps live pointers in unrooted allocas.
(defn mc-walk-ast (ast: Ast) (names: (Map Str Bool)) -> McWalk
  (match ast
    (ParenNode elems _) (mc-walk-paren elems names)
    (BracketNode elems _) (mc-walk-forms elems names)
    (StrNode _ _) (McWalk true [])
    _ (mc-walk-empty)))

; Loop bindings and match patterns look like calls. Walking them would
; mark every arithmetic loop and every match as may-collect. A string
; literal pattern is the exception: it lowers to `mn_str_new`.
(defn mc-walk-loop-inits (pairs: (List Ast)) (names: (Map Str Bool)) -> McWalk
  (match pairs
    [] (mc-walk-empty)
    (Cons p rest)
      (mc-walk-or
        (match (binding-pair-of p)
          (Some [_ init]) (mc-walk-ast init names)
          _ (mc-walk-ast p names))
        (mc-walk-loop-inits rest names))))

(defn mc-walk-loop (rest: (List Ast)) (names: (Map Str Bool)) -> McWalk
  (match rest
    [bindings body]
      (match (binding-list-elems bindings)
        (Some pairs) (mc-walk-or (mc-walk-loop-inits pairs names) (mc-walk-ast body names))
        (None) (mc-walk-or (mc-walk-ast bindings names) (mc-walk-ast body names)))
    _ (mc-walk-forms rest names)))

(defn mc-pat-alloc (pat: Ast) -> Bool
  (match pat
    (StrNode _ _) true
    (ParenNode elems _) (mc-asts-alloc elems)
    (BracketNode elems _) (mc-asts-alloc elems)
    _ false))

(defn mc-asts-alloc (xs: (List Ast)) -> Bool
  (match xs
    [] false
    (Cons p rest) (if (mc-pat-alloc p) true (mc-asts-alloc rest))))

(defn mc-walk-match-clauses (xs: (List Ast)) (names: (Map Str Bool)) -> McWalk
  (match xs
    [] (mc-walk-empty)
    (Cons pat (Cons body rest))
      (mc-walk-or
        (if (mc-pat-alloc pat) (McWalk true []) (mc-walk-empty))
        (mc-walk-or (mc-walk-ast body names) (mc-walk-match-clauses rest names)))
    [other] (mc-walk-ast other names)))

(defn mc-walk-match (rest: (List Ast)) (names: (Map Str Bool)) -> McWalk
  (match rest
    (Cons scrut clauses) (mc-walk-or (mc-walk-ast scrut names) (mc-walk-match-clauses clauses names))
    [] (mc-walk-empty)))

(defn mc-walk-paren (elems: (List Ast)) (names: (Map Str Bool)) -> McWalk
  (match elems
    [] (mc-walk-empty)
    (Cons head rest)
      (match (sym-str head)
        (None) (mc-walk-or (mc-walk-forms rest names) (McWalk true []))
        (Some hn)
          (if (= hn "loop") (mc-walk-loop rest names)
            (if (= hn "match") (mc-walk-match rest names)
              (mc-walk-or (mc-walk-forms rest names) (mc-note-head hn names)))))))

(defn mc-seed (lds: (List LDefn)) -> (Map Str Bool)
  (match lds
    [] (map-new)
    (Cons ld rest) (map-set (mc-seed rest) (ldefn-name ld) false)))

(defn mc-build (lds: (List LDefn)) (names: (Map Str Bool)) -> (Map Str McWalk)
  (match lds
    [] (map-new)
    (Cons ld rest)
      (map-set (mc-build rest names) (ldefn-name ld) (mc-walk-forms (ldefn-body ld) names))))

(defn mc-any-callee (xs: (List Str)) (flags: (Map Str Bool)) -> Bool
  (match xs
    [] false
    (Cons n rest)
      (match (map-get flags n)
        (Some f) (if f true (mc-any-callee rest flags))
        (None) (mc-any-callee rest flags))))

(defn mc-body-true (w: McWalk) (flags: (Map Str Bool)) -> Bool
  (match w
    (McWalk direct callees) (if direct true (mc-any-callee callees flags))))

(defn mc-apply (lds: (List LDefn)) (info: (Map Str McWalk)) (flags: (Map Str Bool)) -> (Map Str Bool)
  (match lds
    [] flags
    (Cons ld rest) (mc-apply-one ld rest info flags)))

(defn mc-apply-one (ld: LDefn) (rest: (List LDefn)) (info: (Map Str McWalk)) (flags: (Map Str Bool)) -> (Map Str Bool)
  (let name (ldefn-name ld))
  (let now (match (map-get flags name) (Some f) f (None) false))
  (let next-flag
    (if now true
      (match (map-get info name)
        (Some w) (mc-body-true w flags)
        (None) true)))
  (mc-apply rest info (map-set flags name next-flag)))

(defn mc-flags-equal (lds: (List LDefn)) (a: (Map Str Bool)) (b: (Map Str Bool)) -> Bool
  (match lds
    [] true
    (Cons ld rest)
      (match (map-get a (ldefn-name ld))
        (None) false
        (Some fa)
          (match (map-get b (ldefn-name ld))
            (None) false
            (Some fb) (if (= fa fb) (mc-flags-equal rest a b) false)))))

(defn mc-propagate (lds: (List LDefn)) (info: (Map Str McWalk)) (flags: (Map Str Bool)) (n: Int) -> (Map Str Bool)
  (if (<= n 0) flags (mc-propagate-step lds info flags n)))

(defn mc-propagate-step (lds: (List LDefn)) (info: (Map Str McWalk)) (flags: (Map Str Bool)) (n: Int) -> (Map Str Bool)
  (let next (mc-apply lds info flags))
  (if (mc-flags-equal lds flags next) next (mc-propagate lds info next (- n 1))))

(defn mc-analyze (lds: (List LDefn)) -> (Map Str Bool)
  (let names (mc-seed lds))
  (mc-propagate lds (mc-build lds names) names (length lds)))

; Imported constructors keep the tag recorded in the dependency's
; interface. Names already in `seeds` are not assigned again, so a leaf
; change cannot renumber a constructor another module already inlined.
(pub defrec CtorSeed (name: Str) (tag: Int) (arity: Int))
(pub defrec CtorTable (specs: (Map Str CtorSpec)) (local: (List CtorSeed)))

(defn seed-specs (seeds: (List CtorSeed)) (acc: (Map Str CtorSpec)) -> (Map Str CtorSpec)
  (match seeds
    [] acc
    (Cons (CtorSeed n t a) rest) (seed-specs rest (map-set acc n (CtorSpec t a)))))

(defn max-seed-tag (seeds: (List CtorSeed)) (acc: Int) -> Int
  (match seeds
    [] acc
    (Cons (CtorSeed _ t _) rest) (if (> t acc) (max-seed-tag rest t) (max-seed-tag rest acc))))

(defn seed-start (seeds: (List CtorSeed)) -> Int
  (let m (+ (max-seed-tag seeds (- user-ctor-tag-base 1)) 1))
  (if (> m user-ctor-tag-base) m user-ctor-tag-base))

(defn reverse-seeds (xs: (List CtorSeed)) (acc: (List CtorSeed)) -> (List CtorSeed)
  (match xs [] acc (Cons x rest) (reverse-seeds rest (Cons x acc))))

(defn note-ctor (acc: (Map Str CtorSpec)) (name: Str) (arity: Int) (tag-ref: (Ref Int)) (local: (Ref (List CtorSeed))) -> (Map Str CtorSpec)
  (match (map-get acc name)
    (Some _) acc
    (None)
      (do
        (let tag (deref tag-ref))
        (set! tag-ref (+ tag 1))
        (set! local (Cons (CtorSeed name tag arity) (deref local)))
        (map-set acc name (CtorSpec tag arity)))))

(defn note-one-variant (c: Ast) (acc: (Map Str CtorSpec)) (tag-ref: (Ref Int)) (local: (Ref (List CtorSeed))) -> (Map Str CtorSpec)
  (match c
    (ParenNode (Cons cname-ast payload) _)
      (match (sym-str cname-ast)
        (None) acc
        (Some name)
          (match (builtin-ctor-tag-of name)
            (Some _) acc
            (None) (note-ctor acc name (length payload) tag-ref local)))
    _ acc))

(defn note-variant-ctors (ctors: (List Ast)) (acc: (Map Str CtorSpec)) (tag-ref: (Ref Int)) (local: (Ref (List CtorSeed))) -> (Map Str CtorSpec)
  (match ctors
    [] acc
    (Cons c rest) (note-variant-ctors rest (note-one-variant c acc tag-ref local) tag-ref local)))

(defn note-defrec (rest: (List Ast)) (acc: (Map Str CtorSpec)) (tag-ref: (Ref Int)) (local: (Ref (List CtorSeed))) -> (Map Str CtorSpec)
  (match rest
    (Cons name-part fields)
      (match (decl-name-of name-part)
        (None) acc
        (Some name)
          (match (builtin-ctor-tag-of name)
            (Some _) acc
            (None) (note-ctor acc name (length fields) tag-ref local)))
    [] acc))

(defn note-ctor-named (hn: Str) (rest: (List Ast)) (acc: (Map Str CtorSpec)) (tag-ref: (Ref Int)) (local: (Ref (List CtorSeed))) -> (Map Str CtorSpec)
  (if (= hn "variant")
    (match rest
      (Cons _ ctors) (note-variant-ctors ctors acc tag-ref local)
      [] acc)
    (if (= hn "defrec") (note-defrec rest acc tag-ref local) acc)))

(defn note-ctor-form (ast: Ast) (acc: (Map Str CtorSpec)) (tag-ref: (Ref Int)) (local: (Ref (List CtorSeed))) -> (Map Str CtorSpec)
  (match (unwrap-pub ast)
    (ParenNode (Cons head rest) _)
      (match (sym-str head)
        (None) acc
        (Some hn) (note-ctor-named hn rest acc tag-ref local))
    _ acc))

(defn note-ctor-forms (forms: (List Ast)) (acc: (Map Str CtorSpec)) (tag-ref: (Ref Int)) (local: (Ref (List CtorSeed))) -> (Map Str CtorSpec)
  (match forms
    [] acc
    (Cons f rest) (note-ctor-forms rest (note-ctor-form f acc tag-ref local) tag-ref local)))

(pub defn ctor-info (forms: (List Ast)) (seeds: (List CtorSeed)) -> CtorTable
  (do
    (let local (ref []))
    (let tag-ref (ref (seed-start seeds)))
    (let specs (note-ctor-forms forms (seed-specs seeds (map-new)) tag-ref local))
    (CtorTable specs (reverse-seeds (deref local) []))))

(defn imp-count (imps: (List Imp)) -> Int
  (match imps [] 0 (Cons _ rest) (+ 1 (imp-count rest))))

; Locals keep the abs ids `build-func-refs` assigned. An import whose
; Menard name is also a local function stays local; its declaration is
; still emitted so the id sequence matches the bitcode writer.
(defn add-imp-refs (imps: (List Imp)) (idx: Int) (acc: (Map Str FuncRef)) -> (Map Str FuncRef)
  (match imps
    [] acc
    (Cons (Imp name _ ar) rest)
      (match (map-get acc name)
        (Some _) (add-imp-refs rest (+ idx 1) acc)
        (None) (add-imp-refs rest (+ idx 1) (map-set acc name (FuncRef idx ar))))))

(defn lower-program-build (word-lds: (List LDefn)) (all-lds: (List LDefn)) (forms: (List Ast)) (triple: Str) (paths: (List Str)) (imports: (List Imp)) (seeds: (List CtorSeed)) -> (Result Str Str)
  (do
    (let extra (collect-non-defn-tops forms))
    (let word-lds2 (replace-main-body word-lds extra))
    (let specs (match (ctor-info forms seeds) (CtorTable s _) s))
    (let pool (str-pool-finalize (collect-str-pool forms paths) specs))
    (let num-strings (str-pool-count pool))
    (let num-funcs (length word-lds2))
    (let nimps (imp-count imports))
    (let funcs0 (build-func-refs word-lds2 (+ num-strings extern-count nimps)))
    (let funcs (add-imp-refs imports (+ num-strings extern-count) funcs0))
    (let noop (collect-noop-names all-lds))
    (let num-globals (+ (* 2 num-strings) extern-count nimps num-funcs))
    (let mc (mc-analyze word-lds2))
    (match (lower-all-funcs word-lds2 num-globals funcs noop pool mc)
      (Ok lfuncs) (Ok (write-module-bc (LlvmModule lfuncs (str-pool-strs pool) imports) triple))
      (Err msg) (Err (str-concat "cannot lower `main`: " msg)))))

(defn lower-program-collected-sep (forms: (List Ast)) (triple: Str) (paths: (List Str)) (imports: (List Imp)) (seeds: (List CtorSeed)) -> (Result Str Str)
  (do
    (let lds (collect-ldefns-all forms))
    (let word-lds (filter-word-ldefns lds))
    (lower-program-build word-lds lds forms triple paths imports seeds)))

; One module, with cross-module calls declared from `imports` and
; constructor tags seeded from dependencies. `main` is optional: a
; library object has none, and the bootstrap object is the only C main.
(pub defn lower-program-sep (forms: (List Ast)) (triple: Str) (paths: (List Str)) (imports: (List Imp)) (seeds: (List CtorSeed)) -> (Result Str Str)
  (lower-program-collected-sep (drop-folded-int-lets (subst-int-constants forms)) triple paths imports seeds))
